{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgko612jUUCUs23tJpUNY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014CEJM7JGFUn8HBfQu5mpUn","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\np='src/content/about.js'; s=open(p).read()\ni=s.index(\"  testing: [\"); j=s.index(\"  credits: [\")\nnew = r\"\"\"  testing: [\n    ['HOW MANY ISSUES DID TESTING CATCH?', '@ISSUES@ logged in tests/ISSUES.md, most of them by the scripted playthrough and the systems suite, a few only by looking at screenshots.'],\n    ['HOW MANY WOULD BE CRITICAL OR GAME BREAKING?', '@CRITICAL@. Among them: no gun visible at all, the windscreen blocking the whole view from the driving seat, a crash when a soldier burned to death inside his own brain tick, the M8 ride never ending, FINISH IT eaten by the melee key, and grass fire eating the entire map.'],\n    ['WHAT WAS THE MOST HELPFUL TEST?', 'The bot that plays M0 through both endings with real keys. It found step-order, input-conflict and state bugs no unit test would have, and it runs in Node in a couple of minutes.'],\n    ['WHAT WAS THE LEAST HELPFUL TEST?', 'Screenshots of menus: they cost about three minutes each on this shared machine and the state checks had already proved what they showed. Screenshots of the world, on the other hand, were essential.'],\n  ],\n  engine: [\n    ['WHAT DID YOU LIKE MOST ABOUT THE ENGINE?', 'Engine.headless. The same game, physics and all, in Node with no GPU, booted in about a second. Models and sounds as checked data came close behind.'],\n    ['DID YOU GET STUCK OR GUESS WRONG?', 'Guessed wrong on rowOf and around, which take other arguments than I assumed, and on model ids that clash with the library. Took the groundFog setting from the plan: a negative top inverts its smoothstep and tints everything, which I found by reading its source.'],\n    ['MOST IMPORTANT THING YOU BUILT YOURSELF?', 'The fire grid and everything hung on it: terrain scars, flora swaps, grass blades, soldiers panicking, tanks going up, the map in ink. Then the action layer and the mission runner.'],\n    ['HARDEST PART OF USING THE ENGINE?', 'It is shaped for a platformer. A first-person open world means replacing the rig step, the pad map and the pointer lock logic. And a press queued in a menu stays alive for 150 ms and leaks into play unless you clear it.'],\n    ['WHAT DID YOU CHANGE IN THE ENGINE, AND WHY?', 'none'],\n    ['ONE THING YOU WOULD CHANGE?', 'A real first-person controller preset with no reserved keys, pad codes kept apart from keyboard codes, and an instanced model helper. And fix groundFog for a top below the camera.'],\n  ],\n  prompt: [\n    ['WHAT DID YOU LIKE MOST ABOUT THIS PROMPT?', 'The plan decided almost everything and said what it had verified, so I could build instead of deciding. Its traps table saved hours. The build order and cut order made the size manageable.'],\n    ['WHAT WAS CONFUSING?', 'The plan calls a line verified that turned out wrong for the look (the fog setting). The kit says modules do not load from file:// while the plan rightly says the bundle does. And the brief asks for file naming by GameTitle and SOURCE without saying how to treat spaces.'],\n    ['WHAT WAS THE HARDEST THING TO DO?', 'Keeping one sim working as host, client and headless server at once, and judging the look at a frame every few seconds on a shared machine. I could not play it by hand at speed, so game feel and balance are the least proven part.'],\n    ['WHAT WOULD YOU CHANGE IN THIS PROMPT?', 'Allow a real-time playtest budget, or say plainly that feel is judged later. Ask for a smaller world or fewer missions if polish matters more than breadth: this scope spreads effort thin. Keep the plan, the traps table and the one test command.'],\n  ],\n\"\"\"\ns=s[:i]+new+s[j:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncat > tools/finish.mjs <<'EOF'\n// Fills the issue counts into About and writes exit-interview.json beside the game's HTML, from one source.\nimport { readFileSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { resolve, basename } from 'node:path';\nconst root = resolve(import.meta.dirname, '..'); process.chdir(root);\nconst lines = readFileSync('tests/ISSUES.md', 'utf8').split('\\n').filter((l) => l.startsWith('- '));\nconst crit = lines.filter((l) => /CRITICAL/.test(l)).length;\nlet src = readFileSync('src/content/about.js', 'utf8');\nsrc = src.replace(/'(@ISSUES@|\\d+)( logged in tests\\/ISSUES\\.md)/, `'${lines.length}$2`).replace(/'(@CRITICAL@|\\d+)(\\. Among them)/, `'${crit}$2`);\nwriteFileSync('src/content/about.js', src);\nconst { ABOUT } = await import(`../src/content/about.js?${Date.now()}`);\nconst get = (k) => ABOUT.source.find((r) => r[0] === k)[1];\nconst out = {\n  sourceInformation: { date: get('DATE'), source: get('SOURCE'), plan: get('PLAN'), genre: get('GENRE'), perspective: get('PERSPECTIVE'), tech: get('TECH'), artDirection: get('ART DIRECTION'), animation: get('ANIMATION'), audio: get('AUDIO'), online: get('ONLINE'), testing: get('TESTING'), research: get('RESEARCH'), environment: get('ENVIRONMENT'), model: get('MODEL'), usage: 'added on import' },\n  testingFeedback: ABOUT.testing.map((r) => r[1]), engineFeedback: ABOUT.engine.map((r) => r[1]), promptFeedback: ABOUT.prompt.map((r) => r[1]),\n  aiHub: { name: 'Far Dry Season', tagline: 'The grass burns whoever lit it', description: 'A first-person war-zone survival shooter in a dying plateau country: guns rust, trucks stall, fever keeps a timetable and grass fire goes where the wind says. A contract story with two endings, plus a four-player Cash Run in a burning mine.', type: 'Game', genre: 'Shooter', source: 'Far Cry 2', series: 'Far Cry', players: '1–4', controls: 'Stick or WASD move, R2 or mouse fire, Square or E use, D-pad Up or M raises the map', tags: ['first-person', 'pixel art', 'co-op', 'versus', 'vehicles', 'story'] },\n};\nwriteFileSync(resolve(root, '..', 'exit-interview.json'), `${JSON.stringify(out, null, 2)}\\n`);\nJSON.parse(readFileSync(resolve(root, '..', 'exit-interview.json'), 'utf8'));\nconsole.log(`issues ${lines.length}, critical ${crit}; ${basename(root)}`);\nEOF\ncat >> tests/ISSUES.md <<'EOF'\n- Standing in the driving seat you looked into the opaque windscreen block: nothing visible ahead (screenshot). CRITICAL.\n- Subtitles were drawn behind stacked prompts (screenshot). Not critical.\n- Charge and bottle counts overlapped the ammo count (screenshot). Not critical.\n- Tap to throw vs hold to plant: a held press threw a bottle and burned the pump before any charge (bot). Not critical.\n- Blasts skipped anything already on a fuse, so a charge couldn't kill a pump that had caught (bot). Not critical.\n- The runner kept talk state between steps, so a later talk step finished itself (bot). CRITICAL.\n- Passive GET OUT prompt counted as a real prompt and blocked leaving the truck (bot). CRITICAL.\n- Four software-rendered copies took too long to say ready; the hub check failed until ready moved to the end of setup (hub suite). CRITICAL for sessions.\nEOF\nnode tools/finish.mjs 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-200; echo \"Feedback text in about.js; tools/finish.mjs writes exit-interview.json and fills counts - rerun it last after final ISSUES.md then build.\" >> ../PROGRESS.md; timeout 100 node tests/suites/static.mjs 2>&1 | cut -c1-200 | tail -6","description":"Write feedback text and exit interview tool; run static checks","timeout":200000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3503,"cache_read_input_tokens":697153,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3503},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98060110-4ead-4574-964f-daef0a492581","uuid":"ba71d63e-511b-489f-bf0a-39becea42381","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:20:20.445Z","request_id":"req_011Cgko5znbo8qwmpECNzk2i","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_014CEJM7JGFUn8HBfQu5mpUn":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\np='src/content/about.js'; s=open(p).read()\ni=s.index(\"  testing: [\"); j=s.index(\"  credits: [\")\nnew = r\"\"\"  testing: [\n    ['HOW MANY ISSUES DID TESTING CATCH?', '@ISSUES@ logged in tests/ISSUES.md, most of them by the scripted playthrough and the systems suite, a few only by looking at screenshots.'],\n    ['HOW MANY WOULD BE CRITICAL OR GAME BREAKING?', '@CRITICAL@. Among them: no gun visible at all, the windscreen blocking the whole view from the driving seat, a crash when a soldier burned to death inside his own brain tick, the M8 ride never ending, FINISH IT eaten by the melee key, and grass fire eating the entire map.'],\n    ['WHAT WAS THE MOST HELPFUL TEST?', 'The bot that plays M0 through both endings with real keys. It found step-order, input-conflict and state bugs no unit test would have, and it runs in Node in a couple of minutes.'],\n    ['WHAT WAS THE LEAST HELPFUL TEST?', 'Screenshots of menus: they cost about three minutes each on this shared machine and the state checks had already proved what they showed. Screenshots of the world, on the other hand, were essential.'],\n  ],\n  engine: [\n    ['WHAT DID YOU LIKE MOST ABOUT THE ENGINE?', 'Engine.headless. The same game, physics and all, in Node with no GPU, booted in about a second. Models and sounds as checked data came close behind.'],\n    ['DID YOU GET STUCK OR GUESS WRONG?', 'Guessed wrong on rowOf and around, which take other arguments than I assumed, and on model ids that clash with the library. Took the groundFog setting from the plan: a negative top inverts its smoothstep and tints everything, which I found by reading its source.'],\n    ['MOST IMPORTANT THING YOU BUILT YOURSELF?', 'The fire grid and everything hung on it: terrain scars, flora swaps, grass blades, soldiers panicking, tanks going up, the map in ink. Then the action layer and the mission runner.'],\n    ['HARDEST PART OF USING THE ENGINE?', 'It is shaped for a platformer. A first-person open world means replacing the rig step, the pad map and the pointer lock logic. And a press queued in a menu stays alive for 150 ms and leaks into play unless you clear it.'],\n    ['WHAT DID YOU CHANGE IN THE ENGINE, AND WHY?', 'none'],\n    ['ONE THING YOU WOULD CHANGE?', 'A real first-person controller preset with no reserved keys, pad codes kept apart from keyboard codes, and an instanced model helper. And fix groundFog for a top below the camera.'],\n  ],\n  prompt: [\n    ['WHAT DID YOU LIKE MOST ABOUT THIS PROMPT?', 'The plan decided almost everything and said what it had verified, so I could build instead of deciding. Its traps table saved hours. The build order and cut order made the size manageable.'],\n    ['WHAT WAS CONFUSING?', 'The plan calls a line verified that turned out wrong for the look (the fog setting). The kit says modules do not load from file:// while the plan rightly says the bundle does. And the brief asks for file naming by GameTitle and SOURCE without saying how to treat spaces.'],\n    ['WHAT WAS THE HARDEST THING TO DO?', 'Keeping one sim working as host, client and headless server at once, and judging the look at a frame every few seconds on a shared machine. I could not play it by hand at speed, so game feel and balance are the least proven part.'],\n    ['WHAT WOULD YOU CHANGE IN THIS PROMPT?', 'Allow a real-time playtest budget, or say plainly that feel is judged later. Ask for a smaller world or fewer missions if polish matters more than breadth: this scope spreads effort thin. Keep the plan, the traps table and the one test command.'],\n  ],\n\"\"\"\ns=s[:i]+new+s[j:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncat > tools/finish.mjs <<'EOF'\n// Fills the issue counts into About and writes exit-interview.json beside the game's HTML, from one source.\nimport { readFileSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { resolve, basename } from 'node:path';\nconst root = resolve(import.meta.dirname, '..'); process.chdir(root);\nconst lines = readFileSync('tests/ISSUES.md', 'utf8').split('\\n').filter((l) => l.startsWith('- '));\nconst crit = lines.filter((l) => /CRITICAL/.test(l)).length;\nlet src = readFileSync('src/content/about.js', 'utf8');\nsrc = src.replace(/'(@ISSUES@|\\d+)( logged in tests\\/ISSUES\\.md)/, `'${lines.length}$2`).replace(/'(@CRITICAL@|\\d+)(\\. Among them)/, `'${crit}$2`);\nwriteFileSync('src/content/about.js', src);\nconst { ABOUT } = await import(`../src/content/about.js?${Date.now()}`);\nconst get = (k) => ABOUT.source.find((r) => r[0] === k)[1];\nconst out = {\n  sourceInformation: { date: get('DATE'), source: get('SOURCE'), plan: get('PLAN'), genre: get('GENRE'), perspective: get('PERSPECTIVE'), tech: get('TECH'), artDirection: get('ART DIRECTION'), animation: get('ANIMATION'), audio: get('AUDIO'), online: get('ONLINE'), testing: get('TESTING'), research: get('RESEARCH'), environment: get('ENVIRONMENT'), model: get('MODEL'), usage: 'added on import' },\n  testingFeedback: ABOUT.testing.map((r) => r[1]), engineFeedback: ABOUT.engine.map((r) => r[1]), promptFeedback: ABOUT.prompt.map((r) => r[1]),\n  aiHub: { name: 'Far Dry Season', tagline: 'The grass burns whoever lit it', description: 'A first-person war-zone survival shooter in a dying plateau country: guns rust, trucks stall, fever keeps a timetable and grass fire goes where the wind says. A contract story with two endings, plus a four-player Cash Run in a burning mine.', type: 'Game', genre: 'Shooter', source: 'Far Cry 2', series: 'Far Cry', players: '1–4', controls: 'Stick or WASD move, R2 or mouse fire, Square or E use, D-pad Up or M raises the map', tags: ['first-person', 'pixel art', 'co-op', 'versus', 'vehicles', 'story'] },\n};\nwriteFileSync(resolve(root, '..', 'exit-interview.json'), `${JSON.stringify(out, null, 2)}\\n`);\nJSON.parse(readFileSync(resolve(root, '..', 'exit-interview.json'), 'utf8'));\nconsole.log(`issues ${lines.length}, critical ${crit}; ${basename(root)}`);\nEOF\ncat >> tests/ISSUES.md <<'EOF'\n- Standing in the driving seat you looked into the opaque windscreen block: nothing visible ahead (screenshot). CRITICAL.\n- Subtitles were drawn behind stacked prompts (screenshot). Not critical.\n- Charge and bottle counts overlapped the ammo count (screenshot). Not critical.\n- Tap to throw vs hold to plant: a held press threw a bottle and burned the pump before any charge (bot). Not critical.\n- Blasts skipped anything already on a fuse, so a charge couldn't kill a pump that had caught (bot). Not critical.\n- The runner kept talk state between steps, so a later talk step finished itself (bot). CRITICAL.\n- Passive GET OUT prompt counted as a real prompt and blocked leaving the truck (bot). CRITICAL.\n- Four software-rendered copies took too long to say ready; the hub check failed until ready moved to the end of setup (hub suite). CRITICAL for sessions.\nEOF\nnode tools/finish.mjs 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-200; echo \"Feedback text in about.js; tools/finish.mjs writes exit-interview.json and fills counts - rerun it last after final ISSUES.md then build.\" >> ../PROGRESS.md; timeout 100 node tests/suites/static.mjs 2>&1 | cut -c1-200 | tail -6","description":"Write feedback text and exit interview tool; run static checks","timeout":200000}}}
