ld build instead of deciding. Its traps table saved hours. The build order and cut order made the size manageable.\n- The plan calls a line verified that turned out wrong for the look (the fog setting). The kit says modules do not load from file:// while the plan rightly says the bundle does. And the brief asks for file naming by GameTitle and SOURCE without saying how to treat spaces.\n- Keeping one sim working as host, client and headless server at once, and judging the look at a frame every few seconds on a shared machine. I could not play it by hand at speed, so game feel and balance are the least proven part.\n- Allow a real-time playtest budget, or say plainly that feel is judged later. Ask for a smaller world or fewer missions if polish matters more than breadth: this scope spreads effort thin. Keep the plan, the traps table and the one test command.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011bBdanZCTFLtspgaEe4g3H","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
