{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkxGUb29gaRrZ4MWhLTN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The gaps the stop check found are closed, and **Far Dry Season** is finished and handed in.\n\n- **Full test run:** `node tests/run.mjs --all` on the final build, with nothing else using a browser, reports **1,682 passed, 0 failed**. That includes all four AI Hub scenarios and the bot finishing both endings.\n- **Hub card screenshot:** taken and reviewed. To hold the card on screen I staged it in-game with a stand-in session, not inside the hub harness; the harness run still tests the card itself, including Enter answering Ready. The shot exposed a clipped countdown, which is fixed, and that fix was followed by the full test run above.\n- **Other screenshots:** I re-shot and looked at the rifle by day and at night, Tibor's rack, the driving view, the ending card, the dev sliders and the storm. The title, held map, dialogue and surgery shots were already reviewed and didn't need re-shooting.\n\nThe earlier Source Information and feedback stand with one correction: testing caught **26 issues, 14 of them critical**. The About screen and `exit-interview.json` both show those numbers.\n\n**Still unproven:**\n- Nobody has played it at full speed, so game feel and balance are the least proven part.\n- The controller was a stand-in, and no one has listened to the audio; I only checked that sounds render non-silent.\n- The surgery scenes work and read as a forearm, a wound and a reaching hand, but they're the roughest visuals, and the pliers were hidden in the frame I checked.\n- Nothing is committed to git.\n\nFiles are in `work/`:\n- `FarDrySeason-FarCry2-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-162030.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`\n- `FarDrySeason-FarCry2-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-162030/` (dev folder, with `DESIGNERS.md` and `tests/ISSUES.md`)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":621,"cache_read_input_tokens":821208,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":621},"output_tokens":646,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98060110-4ead-4574-964f-daef0a492581","uuid":"4997710a-ea81-40af-b08d-59b3d1d01244","timestamp":"2026-11-06T03:20:18.226Z","request_id":"req_011CgkxGUDS2ghFNyWtWWfRw"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.]: The transcript shows the full test run passing (\"1682 passed, 0 failed\") and the hand-in files existing, but it does not show that everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done. The last assistant message itself lists unfinished items: nobody has played the game at full speed, the controller was a stand-in, no one has listened to the audio, and the surgery pliers were hidden in the frame checked. The stop-check feedback had also asked for a hub card screenshot, and the transcript shows the card was taken only in a stand-in staging, not inside the hub harness. The condition therefore cannot be confirmed from the transcript evidence."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98060110-4ead-4574-964f-daef0a492581","uuid":"94729ef4-4c34-4549-a1b7-9594970b0510","timestamp":"2026-11-06T03:20:22.094Z","isSynthetic":true}
