{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgm2NhVHsbWMjmWrds3nT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Far Dry Season** is finished and handed in. On the final build, `node tests/run.mjs --all` reports **1,688 passed, 0 failed**.\n\n**Closed in this last pass:**\n- **Surgery scenes:** I reviewed all four screenshots. The knife and lighter scenes needed fixing, and now the hand holds the blade over the thigh wound and a small flame shows over the burn. The pliers scene shows the tool above the wounded forearm, and the finger scene shows both hands up, though the snap itself isn't clear in a still frame.\n- **Controller prompts:** I looked at the PlayStation and Xbox glyphs on a live screen with several prompts stacked, and they read correctly in both sets.\n\n**Your plan's Done checklist, on the final build:**\n\n| Item | Status |\n|---|---|\n| Title chosen by random pick, shown on the title screen and in `<title>` | Done |\n| Single HTML file runs from `file://` | Done |\n| `--all` reports 0 failed | Done |\n| All four hub scenarios pass, and the game runs outside a session | Done |\n| Bot finishes both endings | Done |\n| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | Done, checked by the static suite |\n| Pad and keyboard prompts | Checked by tests on the main menus and in-game prompts; PlayStation and Xbox art checked by eye on the in-game prompts |\n| Screenshots reviewed | Done, including the card inside the real hub harness |\n| `pixel-engine.js` byte-identical to the kit | Done |\n\n**What this computer can't do:** nobody has played it at full speed, used a physical controller or listened to it. `TASK.md` lists the missing controller and listener and allows stand-ins, which I used: a stub gamepad and measured Web Audio levels. Software rendering rules out full-speed play here, and `PLAN.md` sets frame rate aside and says not to judge the game by real time in a headless browser. So game feel and balance are still unproven by hand; the dev mode sliders are there to tune them.\n\n**Correction to the earlier feedback:** testing caught **29 issues, 15 of them critical**. The About screen and `exit-interview.json` both carry these numbers. Nothing is committed to git.\n\nFiles are in `work/`:\n- `FarDrySeason-FarCry2-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-162030.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`\n- `FarDrySeason-FarCry2-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-162030/` (dev folder, with `DESIGNERS.md`, `tests/ISSUES.md` and the screenshots in `tests/shots/`)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":497,"cache_read_input_tokens":880302,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":497},"output_tokens":729,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98060110-4ead-4574-964f-daef0a492581","uuid":"1821550e-1de0-4ec4-a9e6-5ae11a19fe60","timestamp":"2026-11-06T04:14:12.105Z","request_id":"req_011Cgm2Nh8TC3QWWLCctKKhL"}
