{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgm3CCYb46jCTp4nCcbSx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Far Dry Season** is finished and handed in. On the final build, `node tests/run.mjs --all` reports **1,781 passed, 0 failed, 0 suites unchanged**, meaning all seven suites ran and none were skipped. The earlier `0 passed, 0 failed, 7 suites unchanged` line just meant the runner skipped suites whose code hadn't changed since they last passed.\n\n**Line-by-line audit:** I checked `PLAN.md` section by section and wrote the result, with how each part was verified, to `tests/PLAN-AUDIT.md`. Nothing from the plan's cut list was cut. It records three differences from the plan: some files are merged, scenes use my own small player instead of the engine's `Timeline`, and fires now die out after about 200 m unless relit. Without that last one, a single match burned the whole map and ruined the plot's arc.\n\n**Gaps the audit found, now fixed and tested where a check made sense:**\n- Rocket soldiers now appear in the world.\n- The tracker now works in Cash Run.\n- M7, M8 and the ending now have at least 8 spoken lines each.\n- Mile Forty is now under shells in M8.\n- Patrol trucks now chase you, and their crews get out at 25 m.\n- Dodging soldiers now actually move.\n- In a shared round, clients now hear and see soldiers and other players firing. The test only confirms the data is sent, so nothing has checked this playing on a client.\n- Distant gunfire now has its own sound, and footsteps on wood are in. These are in the game but only lightly tested.\n- The finger snap in surgery now has a test.\n\n**Alternate plans:** the bot had always ignored these, so I added a test that takes each plan through its radio prompt (M3, M4, M5, M7; M6's friend choice is in the playthrough). It caught a real bug: taking Dov's plan in M4 left a second convoy driving. That's fixed.\n\n**What this computer can't do:** nobody has played it at full speed, used a physical controller or listened to it. Software rendering is about a frame a second here, and `PLAN.md` says not to judge the game by real time. `TASK.md` allows stand-ins for the controller and listening, and I used them. Game feel and balance still need a person with a GPU, and dev mode's sliders are there for that.\n\n**Correction to the earlier feedback:** testing caught **31 issues, 16 of them critical**. The About screen and `exit-interview.json` both carry these numbers. Nothing is committed to git.\n\nFiles are in `work/`:\n- `FarDrySeason-FarCry2-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-162030.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`\n- `FarDrySeason-FarCry2-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-162030/` (dev folder, with `DESIGNERS.md`, `tests/PLAN-AUDIT.md`, `tests/ISSUES.md` and the screenshots in `tests/shots/`)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":548,"cache_read_input_tokens":901515,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":548},"output_tokens":715,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98060110-4ead-4574-964f-daef0a492581","uuid":"e06e4729-b0aa-4a5c-946e-daa9b9076d57","timestamp":"2026-11-06T04:24:56.290Z","request_id":"req_011Cgm3CC9WtdZWYPAJh1wLF"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.]: The transcript does not establish that everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done. The audit in tests/PLAN-AUDIT.md was written and the full run reports '1781 passed, 0 failed', but the last message's own gaps remain open: the finger snap is 'not clear in a still frame', surgery and glyph checks were by eye on single frames, the distant-gunfire and wood-footstep sounds are 'only lightly tested', and the client-side gunfire has only been checked for data being sent, not played. The hand-in files exist, but the on-computer PLAN.md completion is not clearly confirmed."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98060110-4ead-4574-964f-daef0a492581","uuid":"7c01e48d-890a-4bcd-a03b-59b05d6d4958","timestamp":"2026-11-06T04:25:00.913Z","isSynthetic":true}
