{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgm5QCvyVxjNfjKFGCga1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Far Dry Season** is finished and handed in, and everything in `PLAN.md` that this computer can do is done. On the final build, `node tests/run.mjs --all` reports **1,842 passed, 0 failed**, with all seven suites run.\n\n**`PLAN.md` section 27, line by line:** `node tests/lib/checklist.mjs` reads the hand-in itself and prints:\n\n```\nPASS  Title in <title> and on the title screen (browser suite passed on this code)\nPASS  One HTML file runs from file:// with nothing beside it (browser suite)\nPASS  --all: every suite last passed on exactly this code: static=ok systems=ok playthrough=ok replay=ok browser=ok hub=ok link=ok\nPASS  All four hub scenarios pass and the game runs outside a session\nPASS  Bot finished both endings\nPASS  No TODOs, placeholders or stubs (static suite scans src/)\nPASS  Every screen: pad PlayStation, pad Xbox, keyboard and mouse prompts (systems suite walks all 17 screens in 3 modes)\nPASS  All ten screenshots the plan lists exist and were reviewed\nPASS  pixel-engine.js byte-identical to the kit\nPASS  About and Credits filled in\nPASS  exit-interview.json parses, right shape, every answer present\n```\n\nThe screenshot line can only check that the files exist; the reviewing was me looking at them during this session. `tests/PLAN-AUDIT.md` covers the rest of the plan section by section, and it was written before these last fixes.\n\n**Closed in this pass:**\n- **Prompts on every screen:** the new test walks 17 screens in all three input modes. It found that the Credits and Results screens showed no button prompt, and both now do.\n- **Sound at the output:** the browser test now taps what the game sends to the speakers after a real key press. The game's own explosion and voice both register there, so this no longer only proves a sound was requested.\n\n**What can't be done on this computer:**\n- **Full-speed play:** software rendering here is about a frame a second, and `PLAN.md` says not to judge the game by real time.\n- **Physical controller and human listening:** `TASK.md` lists both under \"What this computer doesn't have\" and says they are \"never required\", so I used its stand-ins.\n\nGame feel and balance therefore still need a person with a GPU, and dev mode's sliders are there for that. More checks here won't change this, so these stay open as limits of this computer, not unfinished work.\n\n**Correction to the earlier feedback:** testing caught **33 issues, 16 of them critical**. The About screen and `exit-interview.json` both carry these numbers. Nothing is committed to git.\n\nFiles are in `work/`:\n- `FarDrySeason-FarCry2-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-162030.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`\n- `FarDrySeason-FarCry2-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-162030/` (dev folder, with `DESIGNERS.md`, `tests/PLAN-AUDIT.md`, `tests/ISSUES.md` and the screenshots in `tests/shots/`)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":658,"cache_read_input_tokens":928228,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":658},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98060110-4ead-4574-964f-daef0a492581","uuid":"1adfbfd2-e32d-488b-8c90-2c4240f3ad3d","timestamp":"2026-11-06T04:53:53.420Z","request_id":"req_011Cgm5QCYQ4q2BidpDw4hSY"}
