{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgm9AMXicZcpC83GHq5US","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I re-shot the About pages and all ten screenshots the plan lists from the exact final build (the file's checksum didn't change during the batch) and looked at each one. None of them needed a code change, so the **2,019 passed, 0 failed** full test run and the 16-line checklist still apply to what's handed in.\n\n| Screen | What it shows |\n|---|---|\n| **About pages 1 and 6** | All text renders, in the brief's exact question wording, with each answer whole on its page |\n| **Title and main menu** | Title, tagline and menu over the burning field |\n| **Rifle by day** | Rifle, stats and mission text all readable |\n| **Night fire** | Flames across the crop, with Ines beside you and her line subtitled |\n| **Map in a truck** | Held map with subtitles above the prompts |\n| **Tibor's rack and dialogue** | Gun with its stats, and Tibor lit and facing you |\n| **Surgery** | Pliers above the wounded forearm |\n| **Dev sliders** | Tabs and sliders clear, no HUD showing through |\n| **Ending card** | Ending text with a single prompt, no empty bar |\n| **Hub card in the real harness** | Goal, controls, READY and MORE TIME all visible in the narrow frame |\n\nThe one flaw I'm leaving is minor: with the map raised in the truck, the steering wheel overlaps its bottom edge. That doesn't hide anything needed to read the map, and the player's position and waypoint can still be seen.\n\n**Still open:** nobody has played it at full speed, used a physical controller or listened to it. This computer can't do those, as `tests/PLAN-AUDIT.md` records. `TASK.md` says the controller and listening are \"never required\" and gives stand-ins, which I used. Software rendering rules out full-speed play here, so game feel and balance still need a person with a GPU. Further checks here won't change that.\n\nThe Source Information and feedback in my previous message are final and match the About screen and `exit-interview.json` (34 issues, 17 critical). Nothing is committed to git.\n\nFiles are in `work/`:\n- `FarDrySeason-FarCry2-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-162030.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`\n- `FarDrySeason-FarCry2-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-162030/` (dev folder, with `DESIGNERS.md`, `tests/PLAN-AUDIT.md`, `tests/ISSUES.md` and the screenshots in `tests/shots/`)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8632,"cache_read_input_tokens":954444,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8632},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98060110-4ead-4574-964f-daef0a492581","uuid":"f47abc3c-7889-49e5-8e83-24c86c4aa2ec","timestamp":"2026-11-06T05:43:13.686Z","request_id":"req_011Cgm9AMBP8SsX1cusi84UH"}
