{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Read, ScheduleWakeup, TaskStop, ToolSearch</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user's only direct message is the `/goal` command: \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.\" STAGE.md says: \"Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\"\n   - TASK.md: source Far Cry 2; original game only (no recreation); single HTML named `[GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-162030].html`; dev subfolder of the same name; riftlight Pixel Engine kept as shipped; audio all in code with gibberish voices and music at 10%; AI Hub multiplayer; dev mode with sliders; attract mode at 10 s; 10-foot controller-first UI with PlayStation and Xbox glyphs; touch gate text \"Controller or keyboard required\"; Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback in the chat reply and the in-game About screen; `exit-interview.json` beside the HTML.\n   - Constraints that still apply (TASK.md): \"Do not read files outside what you need: other agents work in the folders beside this one.\" Bind servers to 127.0.0.1 on an OS-picked port. \"Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\" Keep one or two browsers open at once. Keep files inside own folder, not /tmp. Don't run `playwright install`. \"Don't use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\" Tests behind one command printing only failures and a one-line count. Git: commit or push only when the user asks. Use the user's email only for identification.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Pixel Engine 0.46.0 (three.js r186, Rapier 0.20, WebGPU), `Engine.headless` for Node tests, esbuild single-file bundle, HUD-only UI (no DOM).\n   - Title \"Far Dry Season\" (random pick from 50 with `secrets.randbelow`).\n   - One Game object with modes (title, attract, play, round); data-driven content; `TUNING` live sliders; actions layer; sim and view apart; 5 m fire grid with generation ageing; mission runner with step types and scripts; hands rigs; AI Hub Session Protocol v1 shared-world with hub, solo and link sessions; host-authoritative netcode.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (all under `work/FarDrySeason-FarCry2-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-162030/`, the dev folder):\n   - `src/game.js` (main game), `src/main.js` (browser boot), `src/core/*`, `src/world/*` (terrain, fire, sky, world, map-texture, geom), `src/actors/*` (rig, soldier, player, buddy, civilian), `src/combat/*` (weapons, projectiles, viewmodel), `src/body/health.js`, `src/vehicles/vehicle.js`, `src/missions/*` (runner, scripts, ledger), `src/ui/*` (hud, menu, glyphs, screens, dialogue, prompts, pixfont), `src/dev/devmode.js`, `src/attract/director.js`, `src/net/*` (session, round), `src/audio/*` (sfx, music, voice, sound), `src/art/*` (models, viewmodels, clips), `src/content/*` (title, weapons, sites, roads, missions, dialogue, about, tuning-defaults).\n   - `tools/build.mjs` (writes the HTML to the parent folder), `tools/finish.mjs` (fills issue counts into about.js from `tests/ISSUES.md`, writes `../exit-interview.json`).\n   - `tests/run.mjs` (one command; `--all`, `--only`; stamps in `tests/.stamps.json`), `tests/suites/{static,systems,playthrough,replay,browser,hub,link}.mjs`, `tests/lib/{boot,bot,artcheck,checklist}.mjs`, `tests/lib/{shots,cardshot}.py`, `tests/ISSUES.md` (34 issues, 17 critical), `tests/PLAN-AUDIT.md` (section-by-section audit, up to date), `tests/shots/*.png`, `DESIGNERS.md`.\n   - Hand-in in `work/`: `FarDrySeason-FarCry2-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-162030.html`, `exit-interview.json`, the dev folder, and `PROGRESS.md`.\n\n4. Errors and fixes (main ones):\n   - Bare `cat > /tmp/x` hung the shell; stopped the task and avoided it afterwards.\n   - `groundFog` with negative `top` tinted everything; now `top: 0.01`.\n   - Gun behind the near plane; opaque windscreen in the driving seat (truck body hidden when seated, dash frame added); gun lowering tipped the map.\n   - Crash on burning death mid-tick; M8 ride never ended (step `end` hooks now run for all script steps); FINISH IT swallowed by melee; fire ate the whole map (fires now tire after about 200 m unless relit, crop exempt); link round never started; four-player hub ready too slow (ready now at end of setup); map click swallowed on foot; auto missions not resumed on load; duplicate M4 convoy on Dov's plan.\n   - Hub card clipped in a narrow frame (now reflows); Credits and Results had no prompts; About page drew body lines wrongly because strings have a built-in `.big` method (now `typeof l === 'object'`), found by extending the checklist.\n   - Audit gaps closed: rocket soldiers, tracker in rounds, at least 8 lines per mission, shells at Mile Forty, far gun sounds, wood steps, patrol chase, dodge movement, client gunfire.\n   - Full run once failed with \"Target crashed\" while screenshots ran beside it (memory); reruns alone pass.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   Final state on the final build: `node tests/run.mjs --all` reported 2,019 passed, 0 failed, 0 suites unchanged. A later `node tests/run.mjs` reported `0 passed, 0 failed, 7 suites unchanged`, meaning all suites are already green on this exact code. `node tests/lib/checklist.mjs` passes all 16 lines. Engine byte-identical to the kit. About pages and all ten screenshots the plan lists were re-shot from the final build (checksum unchanged during the batch, 7e2a8909f524) and reviewed; no code change needed. Known minor flaw left: the steering wheel overlaps the bottom edge of the raised map in the truck. Audit timestamp (22:14) is after the newest source change (22:09) and build (22:11).\n   Not possible on this computer: full-speed play by a person, physical controller, human listening. TASK.md lists the controller and listening under \"What this computer doesn't have\" as never required, with stand-ins, which were used. Game feel and balance remain unproven by hand. Nothing is committed to git.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - `/goal` \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.\"\n   - All later messages were automated: stop-hook feedback restating that the condition is not confirmed (most recent: it says on-computer PLAN.md items are \"not shown as fully verified line by line\" and that suggesting `/goal clear` \"is not completion\"), task notifications, and system reminders. None is a user approval or confirmation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   No unfinished on-computer work is known. The stop hook keeps objecting, but its latest points concern wording of my messages and items already checked; off-computer items can't be closed here.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Final verification and reporting. The last action confirmed the audit is current, the checklist has 16 PASS lines, and the suites are unchanged since the passing `--all` run. The final Source Information and feedback were given in the chat reply and match the About screen and `exit-interview.json` (34 issues, 17 critical).\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   None required. If continuing, report plainly from the evidence above without new claims; only do more work if a concrete on-computer gap in PLAN.md is identified. Any further source change would need `node tools/finish.mjs`, `node tools/build.mjs`, and a fresh `node tests/run.mjs --all` with no other browsers running.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-opus-5-5-medium-build-v2--20261105-162030--x07393c-work/98060110-4ead-4574-964f-daef0a492581.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98060110-4ead-4574-964f-daef0a492581","uuid":"d73c3dde-4099-4322-8c71-ae988773a581","timestamp":"2026-11-06T05:45:32.273Z","isSynthetic":true}
