{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgmJVAgSCXAq1NKmoJnhr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Far Dry Season is finished: every line of the plan's Done list passes on the final build (`b81fac8e7b13`), and all the hand-ins `TASK.md` asks for are in this folder.** What's left can't be done on this computer: a person playing it at full speed, a real controller, and listening by ear. `TASK.md` doesn't require the last two here, so I used its stand-ins.\n\n## Results on the final build\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Full test run, `node tests/run.mjs --all` | 2,298 passed, 0 failed |\n| Plan requirements, in `tests/PLAN-LINES.txt` | 279 passed, 0 failed |\n| The plan's Done list, in `tests/lib/checklist.mjs` | 16 of 16 pass |\n| Screenshots | all 17 re-shot from this build; I looked at 16 |\n| Exit interview | parses as JSON |\n\nThe one screenshot I didn't look at again is About page 6, which I reviewed on the build before last. Nothing on that page has changed since.\n\n## What changed in this pass\n- **Map text:** the map is now drawn at about full size, so all its lettering reads, including the small margin text. It's bigger on screen, so the objective line now sits on its top edge.\n- **Balance:** a bot now measures it, and the suite fails if a number leaves its range:\n\n| Situation | Measured |\n|---|---|\n| 1 rifleman at 35 m | 17.6 s to cost you 75 HP |\n| 3 riflemen at 35 m | 6.9 s |\n| 6 riflemen at 35 m | 6.6 s |\n| `m38` pistol at 15 m | 3 shots to kill |\n| `tractor` rifle at 30 m | 8 shots |\n| `mule` pump gun at 12 m | 1.7 shots |\n| `empire` rifle, scoped, at 60 m | 1 shot |\n\n- **How far to trust those numbers:**\n    - I chose the ranges myself, and the plan doesn't give any.\n    - Each figure averages only three runs, so they're noisy; an earlier run had six riflemen nearer 4 s.\n    - They show nothing is badly broken, not that the game feels right.\n\nNo code changed from the balance measurements. Nothing is committed to git, as you didn't ask for a commit.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-05 16:20:30\n- **Source:** Far Cry 2\n- **Plan:** `PLAN.md`\n- **Genre and Perspective:** open-world first-person shooter with survival pressure and systemic fire; first person on foot, at the wheel and in scenes, with an optional chase camera in vehicles\n- **Tech:** Pixel Engine 0.46.0 (riftlight kit), three.js r186, Rapier 0.20, WebGPU, JavaScript modules bundled with esbuild 0.28 into one HTML file; AI Hub session client 1.4.0\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native 3D-as-pixel-art at 480x270, toon materials, 16-colour palette; about 90 new models as data, plus library props\n- **Animation:** the engine's ClipDef system, compileClips and AnimationMixer; hero clips reused, new people clips, a hands rig with surgery scenes; Ragdoll on death; procedural sway\n- **Audio:** all in code: SoundDef effects, Song music (7 pieces, music 10% by default), Animalese-style gibberish voices, spatial ambience; no audio files\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world, 1 to 4 players; on its own, solo with AI mercs or two windows on one computer\n- **Testing:** headless Node suites, scripted playthrough, Playwright Chromium on file://, a stand-in gamepad, a phone profile, the hub harness; one command; few screenshots\n- **Research:** none beyond the plan, the engine kit's docs and the hub's README\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** added on import\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** 39 logged in `tests/ISSUES.md`, most of them by the scripted playthrough and the systems suite, a few only by looking at screenshots.\n- **Critical or game-breaking:** 17. They include no gun visible at all, the windscreen blocking the whole view from the driving seat, a crash when a soldier burned to death in the middle of their own AI update, the M8 ride never ending, FINISH IT eaten by the melee key, and grass fire eating the entire map.\n- **Most helpful test:** the bot that plays M0 through both endings with real keys. It found step-order, input-conflict and state bugs no unit test would have, and it runs in Node in a couple of minutes.\n- **Least helpful test:** screenshots of menus. They cost about three minutes each on this shared machine, and the state checks had already proved what they showed. Screenshots of the world, on the other hand, were essential.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** `Engine.headless`: the same game, physics and all, in Node with no GPU, booted in about a second. Models and sounds as checked data came close behind.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** I guessed wrong on `rowOf` and `around`, which take other arguments than I assumed, and on model ids that clash with the library. I also took the `groundFog` setting from the plan; a negative `top` inverts its smoothstep and tints everything, which I found by reading its source.\n- **Most important thing built:** the fire grid and everything hung on it: terrain scars, flora swaps, grass blades, soldiers panicking, tanks going up, the map in ink. Then the action layer and the mission runner.\n- **Hardest part:** it is shaped for a platformer. A first-person open world means replacing the rig step, the pad map and the pointer lock logic. A press queued in a menu also stays alive for 150 ms and leaks into play unless you clear it.\n- **Changed in the engine:** none.\n- **One change:** a real first-person controller preset with no reserved keys, pad codes kept apart from keyboard codes, and an instanced model helper. Also fix `groundFog` for a `top` below the camera.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the plan decided almost everything and said what it had verified, so I could build instead of deciding. Its traps table saved hours, and the build order and cut order made the size manageable.\n- **Confusing:** the plan calls a line verified that turned out wrong for the look (the fog setting). The kit says modules do not load from file://, while the plan rightly says the bundle does. The brief also asks for file naming by GameTitle and SOURCE without saying how to treat spaces.\n- **Hardest:** keeping one sim working as host, client and headless server at once, and judging the look at a frame every few seconds on a shared machine. I could not play it by hand at speed, so game feel and balance are the least proven part.\n- **Would change:** allow a real-time playtest budget, or say plainly that feel is judged later. Ask for a smaller world or fewer missions if polish matters more than breadth, because this scope spreads effort thin. Keep the plan, the traps table and the one test command.\n\n## Files are in `work/`\n- `FarDrySeason-FarCry2-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-162030.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`\n- `FarDrySeason-FarCry2-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-162030/` (dev files; `node tests/run.mjs` runs the tests)\n- `PROGRESS.md`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4025,"cache_read_input_tokens":132288,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4025},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98060110-4ead-4574-964f-daef0a492581","uuid":"cddd9d3d-f9a0-44dd-bada-45256c120bbe","timestamp":"2026-11-06T07:45:41.454Z","request_id":"req_011CgmJV99R9foNcT2saupDF"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.]: The transcript shows the hand-in files exist and the full suite and plan-line checks pass on build b81fac8e7b13. But the condition requires everything in PLAN.md that can be done here to be done, and the transcript does not establish that. The final reply itself says the one About page 6 screenshot was not looked at again and relies on the build-before-last review. It also says the balance ranges were chosen by the agent because the plan gives none, the balance figures average only three noisy runs, and game feel is unproven. The Done checklist is a self-check of its own items, not proof that every PLAN.md section is complete on this build."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98060110-4ead-4574-964f-daef0a492581","uuid":"e8380431-2b83-45ef-842b-86728eafc9e6","timestamp":"2026-11-06T07:45:44.016Z","isSynthetic":true}
