{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MpU6kTeZb1KmgSoG5XXQ1L","type":"tool_result","content":"900:**Base:** the engine's native system. `ClipDef` data at 30 fps, `compileClips`, `THREE.AnimationMixer`, `gaitClip` for walks and runs, `Ragdoll`, `SpringChain`, `Squash`, `twoBoneIK`, tweens for small things, `Timeline` for scenes.\n919:**Scenes:** use `Timeline` for the M0 ride, the rescue drag, M9, and endings, as `cam.override` plus `lines` and `bars()`. Skip with Cross/Enter (`timeline.skip()`).\n---\n222:## 4. Architecture\n241:src/ui/                   hud.js menu.js screens/*.js glyphs.js prompts.js dialogue.js pixfont.js touchgate.js about.js\n712:- `src/ui/glyphs.js` is pixel art as `hud.sprite` rows, about 11 × 11: Cross, Circle, Square, Triangle, L1, L2, R1, R2, L3, R3, D-pad directions, Options, Create; Xbox A, B, X, Y, LB, LT, RB, RT, LS, RS, Menu, View; \n894:**Style rules that matter here:** thin parts must be at least 0.06 m and silhouette parts 0.12 m at world scale, but first-person models are held 0.5 m from the eye, so they may be thinner. Set `floats:true`, `collid\n---\n11:Contents: 1 The game · 2 Setting, cast, story · 3 Verified engine facts · 4 Architecture · 5 World · 6 Fire, wind, time, weather · 7 Player · 8 Weapons and wear · 9 The body · 10 Soldiers and AI · 11 Vehicles · 12 Buddies · 13 Stones, safehouses, side conte\n73:**The twist.** Harrow paid for your contract himself. He is dying of the same fever. Each burn he steered you toward (the East Siding, the Cut, the Long Field) lies on one arc across the Kettle: a firebreak. Burned grass cannot burn twice, so a refugee colu\n87:The kit's guide is written with a platformer in mind. These are the traps and answers for a first-person open-world game. I ran these unless a line says \"not run\". Read `GUIDE.md` whole as the kit asks, and `ASSETS.md` before writing models; search `API.md`\n222:## 4. Architecture\n286:**Sites.** All in `src/content/sites.js` as data. Tune positions by eye; the arc of the East Siding, the Cut, the Long Field and the Pass is the one thing that must stay (it's the plot).\n349:- **A test must measure the head of the fire at wind 5 m/s and require 2 to 5 m/s,** with flanks clearly slower, so a sprinting or running player can escape and a walking one (3.6 m/s) struggles.\n428:| `flare` | Flare pistol | sidearm | 1 / 8 | 0.6/s | 12 + ignite | arcs to 70 m | 0 | given in M3 | Gravity projectile; lights fuel where it lands; sets soldiers alight |\n438:Hip fire has a small spread; L2/RMB aims (FOV 62 to 45; `empire` to 12) with tighter spread and recoil. Hitscan for bullets using `physics.castRay`, with the collider-to-actor map from section 10; rockets, flares and bottles are projectiles integrated per","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98060110-4ead-4574-964f-daef0a492581","uuid":"bdc2a717-47f2-4add-a775-b1ae5367dfe3","timestamp":"2026-11-06T07:46:34.156Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"900:**Base:** the engine's native system. `ClipDef` data at 30 fps, `compileClips`, `THREE.AnimationMixer`, `gaitClip` for walks and runs, `Ragdoll`, `SpringChain`, `Squash`, `twoBoneIK`, tweens for small things, `Timeline` for scenes.\n919:**Scenes:** use `Timeline` for the M0 ride, the rescue drag, M9, and endings, as `cam.override` plus `lines` and `bars()`. Skip with Cross/Enter (`timeline.skip()`).\n---\n222:## 4. Architecture\n241:src/ui/                   hud.js menu.js screens/*.js glyphs.js prompts.js dialogue.js pixfont.js touchgate.js about.js\n712:- `src/ui/glyphs.js` is pixel art as `hud.sprite` rows, about 11 × 11: Cross, Circle, Square, Triangle, L1, L2, R1, R2, L3, R3, D-pad directions, Options, Create; Xbox A, B, X, Y, LB, LT, RB, RT, LS, RS, Menu, View; \n894:**Style rules that matter here:** thin parts must be at least 0.06 m and silhouette parts 0.12 m at world scale, but first-person models are held 0.5 m from the eye, so they may be thinner. Set `floats:true`, `collid\n---\n11:Contents: 1 The game · 2 Setting, cast, story · 3 Verified engine facts · 4 Architecture · 5 World · 6 Fire, wind, time, weather · 7 Player · 8 Weapons and wear · 9 The body · 10 Soldiers and AI · 11 Vehicles · 12 Buddies · 13 Stones, safehouses, side conte\n73:**The twist.** Harrow paid for your contract himself. He is dying of the same fever. Each burn he steered you toward (the East Siding, the Cut, the Long Field) lies on one arc across the Kettle: a firebreak. Burned grass cannot burn twice, so a refugee colu\n87:The kit's guide is written with a platformer in mind. These are the traps and answers for a first-person open-world game. I ran these unless a line says \"not run\". Read `GUIDE.md` whole as the kit asks, and `ASSETS.md` before writing models; search `API.md`\n222:## 4. Architecture\n286:**Sites.** All in `src/content/sites.js` as data. Tune positions by eye; the arc of the East Siding, the Cut, the Long Field and the Pass is the one thing that must stay (it's the plot).\n349:- **A test must measure the head of the fire at wind 5 m/s and require 2 to 5 m/s,** with flanks clearly slower, so a sprinting or running player can escape and a walking one (3.6 m/s) struggles.\n428:| `flare` | Flare pistol | sidearm | 1 / 8 | 0.6/s | 12 + ignite | arcs to 70 m | 0 | given in M3 | Gravity projectile; lights fuel where it lands; sets soldiers alight |\n438:Hip fire has a small spread; L2/RMB aims (FOV 62 to 45; `empire` to 12) with tighter spread and recoil. Hitscan for bullets using `physics.castRay`, with the collider-to-actor map from section 10; rockets, flares and bottles are projectiles integrated per","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MpU6kTeZb1KmgSoG5XXQ1L","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
