{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YQBy7MC3CkXCRaaQSVBPDE","type":"tool_result","content":"### class Timeline\n\n- `new Timeline(o: TimelineOptions)`\n- `readonly duration: number`\n- `time: number`: The playhead (s).\n- `playing: boolean`\n- `speed: number`: Playback rate (1: real time, 0.5: slow motion).\n- `ended: boolean`: True once the end has been reached (by playing or skipping).\n- `readonly fired: string[]`: Cue names in the order they fired (tests and tools).\n- `play(): void`\n- `pause(): void`\n- `update(dt: number): void`: Advance by `dt` seconds of game time (times `speed`) while playing, firing the cues passed.\n- `seek(t: number): void`: Move the playhead to `t` without firing the cues in between (scrubbing). Cues before `t` count as done and cues after it will fire again (going back re-arms them). Ignored while skipping (a cue that loops back cannot undo a skip).\n- `skip(): void`: Jump to the end: the cues not yet fired run (except the cosmetic ones), then `onEnd`. Cues after `duration` never fire, played or skipped.\n- `camera(t = this.time): CameraShot | null`: Where the camera is at `t` (default now): on each key at its time, gliding between keys on a smooth curve (Catmull-Rom tangents, so the speed has no jolt at a key; the first and last key of each shot ease in and ou\n- `line(t = this.time): Line | null`: The subtitle showing at `t` (default now), or null.\n- `bars(t = this.time): number`: How far the letterbox bars are in (0..1) at `t` (default now): sliding in at the start, out at the end.\n\n### interface TimelineLine\n\n- `at: number`\n- `until: number`\n- `text: string`\n- `who?: string`: Who is speaking (shown before the text).\n\n### interface TimelineOptions\n\n- `shots?: readonly CameraKey[]`\n- `cues?: readonly Cue[]`\n- `lines?: readonly Line[]`\n- `duration?: number`: Length (s); default the last key, cue or line.\n- `bars?: number`: Seconds the letterbox bars take to slide in and out (default 0.6; 0: no bars).\n- `onEnd?: () => void`: Called once when the playhead reaches the end (or the scene is skipped).\n\n### interface TraceRow\n\n- `name: string`\n- `kind: string`\n- `depth: number`\n- `status: Status | null`: This tick's answer, or null if this tick never reached the node.\n\n### class Trail\n\n- `new Trail(o: TrailOptions = {})`\n- `readonly capacity: number`\n4049:### interface CameraKey\n4050-\n4051-- `at: number`: Time (s) the camera is exactly here.\n4052-- `position: V3`\n4053-- `target: V3`: The point it looks at.\n4054-- `fov?: number`: Vertical field of view (degrees); default the previous key's, or 50.\n4055-- `cut?: boolean`: Jump here instead of gliding from the key before (a cut to a new shot).\n4056-\n4057-### class CameraShake\n4058-\n4059-- `trauma: number`\n4060-- `maxOffset: number`: World units at full trauma.\n4061-- `decay: number`: Trauma lost per second.\n--\n4071:### interface CameraShot\n4072-\n4073-- `position: [number, number, number]`\n4074-- `target: [number, number, number]`\n4075-- `fov: number`\n4076-\n4077-### interface ClockState\n4078-\n4079-A clock as data.\n4080-\n4081-- `readonly scale: number`\n4082-- `readonly hitstop: number`\n4083-\n--\n4107:### interface Cue\n4108-\n4109-- `at: number`\n4110-- `name?: string`\n4111-- `run: () => void`\n4112-- `cosmetic?: boolean`: Cosmetic (a sound, a puff of dust): not run when the scene is skipped past it. Cues that change the world (a door left open, an item given) are run on skip so the world en\n4113-\n4114-### DECAL_SHAPES\n4115-\n4116-```ts\n4117-const DECAL_SHAPES: readonly [\"footprint\", \"scorch\", \"splat\", \"crack\", \"ring\"]\n4118-```\n466:- `TUNING.feverMinutes` (default 12) ± 2 between attacks; the interval shrinks by 1 minute after each act. First attack scripted in M0.\n605:Contracts are taken in person (a short FP scene: the camera holds on the giver, subtitles, then Accept or Not Yet) or through the notice board in Mile Forty. After M2, the order within M3/M4 and M5/M6 is free; M5 needs M3 and M6 needs M4 (one faction's path each); M7 needs all four. Acts, for the fever's pace: act 1 is M0 to M2, act 2 is M3 to M6, act 3 is M7 onward.\n609:| M0 | The Goods Line | 2 min, dusk, skippable | You ride Old Bakr's flatcar into the Kettle as he talks. Prompt: raise the map (must do). The margin note. Fever on the platform; you fall | Look, map | - | Fade to the clinic |\n641:- **Bakr, M0:** *Forty miles of track and not one station that remembers its name.* / *They paint the signs over. Whoever won last.* / *You have the look of a man who read about this place. Reading is a good way to visit.* / *Up there they will ask you which side. Say yes.*\n919:**Scenes:** use `Timeline` for the M0 ride, the rescue drag, M9, and endings, as `cam.override` plus `lines` and `bars()`. Skip with Cross/Enter (`timeline.skip()`).\n// The scripted beats of the story. Everything else in missions.js is plain data.\nimport { LINES } from '../content/dialogue.js';\nimport { RAILWAY, ROADS } from '../content/roads.js';\nimport { siteById } from '../content/sites.js';\nimport { TUNING } from '../core/tuning.js';\nimport { dist2, polyPoint } from '../world/geom.js';\nimport { BURNING, BURNT, cellX, cellZ, FIRE_N } from '../world/fire.js';\nconst fieldProgress = (g) => { const f = g.world.fire, site = siteById['long-field']; let tot = 0, lit = 0; const x0 = site.at[0] - 90, z0 = site.at[1] - 60; for (let z = z0; z < z0 + 120; z += 5) for (let x = x0; x < x0\nexport const SCRIPTS = {\n  // ----- M0 -----\n  m0Ride: {\n6:    steps: [{ do: 'ride', script: 'm0Ride', seconds: 38, text: 'RIDE THE GOODS LINE', lines: 'm0.ride' }, { do: 'script', script: 'm0Map', text: 'RAISE YOUR MAP' }, { do: 'script', script: 'm0Fever', text: 'GET OFF THE TRAIN', lines: 'm0.after' }],\n88:      { do: 'script', script: 'm9Scene', text: 'LOOK AT THE MAP', lines: 'm9.scene' },\n76:export function endingScreen(g) {\n77-  const text = ENDINGS[g.story.ending ?? 'walk'];