{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgmQMGTfnstJrEKEvFMdL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Rh5KWWz13MsVmdFo3Mufos","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 250,256p ../PLAN.md | cut -c1-260; sed -n 900,918p ../PLAN.md | cut -c1-330; for k in \"function gaitClip\" \"class SpringChain\" \"class Squash\" \"function twoBoneIK\" \"interface GaitClipOptions\\|interface GaitOptions\" \"interface SpringChainOptions\" \"interface SquashOptions\"; do echo \"=== $k\"; grep -n -E \"### .*($k)|$k\" API.md | head -2 | cut -c1-200; done; for w in gaitClip SpringChain Squash twoBoneIK; do L=$(grep -n \"### .*\\b$w\\b\" API.md | head -1 | cut -d: -f1); [ -n \"$L\" ] && sed -n \"$L,$((L+14))p\" API.md | cut -c1-280; done; grep -n -i -E \"gaitClip|SpringChain|new Squash|twoBoneIK\" GUIDE.md | cut -c1-360 | head -8; wc -l src/actors/rig.js src/art/clips.js; sed -n 1,30p src/actors/rig.js | cut -c1-200; grep -n -E \"Walk|Run\" src/art/clips.js | cut -c1-180 | head -10","description":"Read plan layout wording and the animation APIs"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3033,"cache_read_input_tokens":215524,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3033},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98060110-4ead-4574-964f-daef0a492581","uuid":"005a5c42-e03b-4232-9ac5-209527cccd8d","timestamp":"2026-11-06T09:02:27.893Z","request_id":"req_011CgmQMG7qFy5pR5nDCxjFv","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Rh5KWWz13MsVmdFo3Mufos":{"command":"sed -n 250,256p ../PLAN.md | cut -c1-260; sed -n 900,918p ../PLAN.md | cut -c1-330; for k in \"function gaitClip\" \"class SpringChain\" \"class Squash\" \"function twoBoneIK\" \"interface GaitClipOptions\\|interface GaitOptions\" \"interface SpringChainOptions\" \"interface SquashOptions\"; do echo \"=== $k\"; grep -n -E \"### .*($k)|$k\" API.md | head -2 | cut -c1-200; done; for w in gaitClip SpringChain Squash twoBoneIK; do L=$(grep -n \"### .*\\b$w\\b\" API.md | head -1 | cut -d: -f1); [ -n \"$L\" ] && sed -n \"$L,$((L+14))p\" API.md | cut -c1-280; done; grep -n -i -E \"gaitClip|SpringChain|new Squash|twoBoneIK\" GUIDE.md | cut -c1-360 | head -8; wc -l src/actors/rig.js src/art/clips.js; sed -n 1,30p src/actors/rig.js | cut -c1-200; grep -n -E \"Walk|Run\" src/art/clips.js | cut -c1-180 | head -10","description":"Read plan layout wording and the animation APIs"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rh5KWWz13MsVmdFo3Mufos","type":"tool_result","content":"**Patterns to follow:**\n- **One Game object, one Engine.** `createGame()` builds the world once. Title, attract, campaign and round are modes on it (`game.mode`). Don't use `engine.loadGame` between them: it would throw away the terrain. For New Game and Attract use `world.reset()`, \n- **Data over code.** All content lives in `src/content/` and `src/art/` as plain data. Adding a weapon, site, mission, line of dialogue or model must not need a code change. This is what lets the rest of the game be built later \"with normal designer tools\": t\n- **Actions, not keys.** `src/core/actions.js` maps an action to its pad code and its keyboard/mouse codes (section 16). All gameplay asks for actions. In `fixedUpdate` use `input.consumeAny(codes)`; in `update` use `wasPressed`.\n- **Gameplay in `fixedUpdate`, presentation in `update`.** All randomness comes from `ctx.random.fork(name)`, never `Math.random`. Cosmetic forks are made in `setup`.\n- **`TUNING`.** Every balance number lives in `src/content/tuning-defaults.js`, copied to a live `TUNING` object. Systems read `TUNING.x` at the moment of use and never cache it, so sliders act instantly.\n**Base:** the engine's native system. `ClipDef` data at 30 fps, `compileClips`, `THREE.AnimationMixer`, `gaitClip` for walks and runs, `Ragdoll`, `SpringChain`, `Squash`, `twoBoneIK`, tweens for small things, `Timeline` for scenes.\n\n**From `HERO_CLIPS`, reused on all people:** Idle, IdleLook, Walk, Run, Crouch, CrouchWalk, Crawl, Sit, SitDown, StandUp, LieIdle, Sleep, Hurt, HitReact, Death, Wave, Shout, Push, Climb. `analyzeClip` and `validateClip` check your own.\n\n**New, on the people rig** (`src/art/clips.js`):\n- **Upper-body, armed versions:** AimIdle, AimWalk (arms holding the rifle, played over the legs), FireRecoil, Reload, ThrowBottle.\n- **New whole-body clips:** BurnPanic (arms flailing, a stumbling run), Beg, Surrender, WoundedSit (clutching a side), DragBackward, CarryOver, DriveSit, UnjamSwear, WalkHandsTied, Shrug (Tibor), SmokeIdle (Odile), CleanRifleIdle (Vance), WriteAtDesk (Harrow), TeachPoint (Ansa).\n\n**To layer upper over lower,** split clips by filtering tracks: `new THREE.AnimationClip(name, clip.duration, clip.tracks.filter(t => /^(Pelvis|Leg|Shin|Foot)/.test(t.name)))`, and the rest for the upper body, then play one of each.\n\n**New, on the hands rig** (`src/art/viewmodels.js` + clips):\n- Idle sway and walk bob (procedural), ADS raise, fire kick per gun.\n- Reload per gun (magazine out and in on `Mag`, bolt on `Bolt`; revolver opens; shells for `mule`; flare breaks open).\n- **Unjam** (slap and rack), **falls apart**, equip and holster.\n- Cane knife swing, throw, plant, detonator click.\n- Tablet to mouth, syrette, **four surgery scenes**, **raise map** and tracker, monocular, wrench on bonnet, hand on wheel and shifter, finish-it.\n\n**Fauna:** gazelle run and graze on its own rig; vulture wing flap.\n\n=== function gaitClip\n3637:function gaitClip(rig: RigSpec, g: GaitSpec): ClipDef\n=== class SpringChain\n3795:### class SpringChain\n=== class Squash\n3817:### class Squash\n=== function twoBoneIK\n3836:function twoBoneIK(root: Vec3, target: Vec3, a: number, b: number, pole: Vec3, out: Vec3 = [0, 0, 0]): Vec3\n=== interface GaitClipOptions\\|interface GaitOptions\n=== interface SpringChainOptions\n3808:### interface SpringChainOptions\n=== interface SquashOptions\n### gaitClip()\n\n```ts\nfunction gaitClip(rig: RigSpec, g: GaitSpec): ClipDef\n```\n\n### gaitPartners()\n\n```ts\nfunction gaitPartners(n: number): number[][]\n```\n\nPartners for `n` legs in two rows (left 0, 2, 4…, right 1, 3, 5…): a leg waits for the legs beside and opposite it.\n\n### interface GaitSpec\n### class SpringChain\n\nA chain of points hanging off a moving root. Call `update(dt, root, basis)` every frame\nwith the root's world position and its orientation (three columns: right, up, forward),\nthen read `points` (root first).\n\n- `new SpringChain(o: SpringChainOptions)`\n- `readonly points: Vec3[]`\n- `o: Required<SpringChainOptions>`\n- `reset(root: Vec3, basis: readonly [Vec3, Vec3, Vec3]): void`: Put the chain straight out in its rest pose (no swing).\n- `update(dt: number, root: Vec3, basis: readonly [Vec3, Vec3, Vec3]): void`\n- `swing(basis: readonly [Vec3, Vec3, Vec3]): number`: How far the tip is from where the rest pose puts it (m): how much it is swinging.\n\n### interface SpringChainOptions\n\n### class Squash\n\nSquash and stretch as a damped spring on `value` (0 = rest, + stretched, − squashed).\n`scale()` turns it into a volume-preserving pair: `const [h, v] = squash.scale();\nmesh.scale.set(h, v, h)`.\n\n- `value: number`\n- `velocity: number`\n- `stiffness: number`: Spring stiffness and damping (a critically damped spring has damping = 2√stiffness).\n- `damping: number`\n- `amount: number`: 0 turns it off; 2.5 is rubbery.\n- `kick(v: number): void`: Add a kick: negative squashes (a landing), positive stretches (a jump).\n- `set(v: number): void`: Set the shape directly (a held squash).\n- `update(dt: number): void`\n- `scale(out: [number, number] = [1, 1]): [number, number]`: [horizontal, vertical] scale: y = 1 + s, xz = 1 / √(1 + s), so the volume stays put.\n### twoBoneIK()\n\n```ts\nfunction twoBoneIK(root: Vec3, target: Vec3, a: number, b: number, pole: Vec3, out: Vec3 = [0, 0, 0]): Vec3\n```\n\nWhere the middle joint of a two-bone limb goes (a knee, an elbow) so the end reaches\n`target` from `root` with bones `a` and `b` long, bending toward `pole` (a point the knee\npoints at). Analytic (the law of cosines), no iterations; a target out of reach straightens\nthe limb toward it, one too close folds it as far as it goes. Returns the joint, into `out`.\n\n### validateClip()\n\n```ts\nfunction validateClip(clip: ClipDef, rig: RigSpec): string[]\n352:const tail = new SpringChain({ segments: 6, length: 0.12 });   // tail.update(dt, root, [right, up, forward]); tail.points\n353:const squash = new Squash();                                   // squash.kick(-5); squash.update(dt); squash.scale() → [xz, y]\n355:legs.update(dt, body, yaw, velocity, (x, z) => 0);             // legs.feet[i].at; knee = twoBoneIK(hip, foot, a, b, pole)\n   59 src/actors/rig.js\n  113 src/art/clips.js\n  172 total\n// A person's view: model on the hero rig, shared compiled clips, layered upper and lower body, ragdoll on death.\nimport { buildModel, compileClips, HERO_CLIPS, HERO_RAGDOLL, HERO_RIG, Ragdoll, setLookLayer, THREE } from '../../pixel-engine.js';\nimport { CATALOG } from '../art/models.js';\nimport { PEOPLE_CLIPS } from '../art/clips.js';\nconst { AnimationClip, AnimationMixer, LoopOnce, LoopRepeat } = THREE;\nlet CLIPS = null, LOWER = null, UPPER = null;\nconst LEGS = /^(Pelvis|Leg|Shin|Foot)/;\nconst KEEP = ['Idle', 'IdleLook', 'Walk', 'Run', 'Crouch', 'CrouchWalk', 'Crawl', 'Sit', 'SitDown', 'StandUp', 'LieIdle', 'Sleep', 'Hurt', 'HitReact', 'Death', 'Wave', 'Shout', 'Push', 'Climb'];\nexport const RIG = { ...HERO_RIG, spine: undefined };\nfunction compile(object) {\n  if (CLIPS) return;\n  const defs = [...HERO_CLIPS.filter((c) => KEEP.includes(c.name)), ...PEOPLE_CLIPS];\n  const all = compileClips(defs, RIG, object);\n  CLIPS = {}; LOWER = {}; UPPER = {};\n  for (const c of all) {\n    CLIPS[c.name] = c;\n    LOWER[c.name] = new AnimationClip(`${c.name}:L`, c.duration, c.tracks.filter((t) => LEGS.test(t.name)));\n    UPPER[c.name] = new AnimationClip(`${c.name}:U`, c.duration, c.tracks.filter((t) => !LEGS.test(t.name)));\n  }\n}\nexport const clipNames = () => Object.keys(CLIPS ?? {});\nexport class PersonView {\n  constructor(ctx, modelId, palette, { gun = false } = {}) {\n    this.ctx = ctx;\n    const b = buildModel(modelId, { catalog: CATALOG, palette });\n    this.object = b.object;\n    compile(b.object);\n    setLookLayer(this.object, 'actors');\n    b.object.traverse((o) => { if (o.isMesh) { o.castShadow = true; o.frustumCulled = false; } });\n    ctx.scene.add(this.object);\n8:  { name: 'AimWalk', frames: 24, loop: true, keys: [K(0, merge(AIM, { Torso: [8, -16, 2] })), K(12, merge(AIM, { Torso: [8, -12, -2] })), K(24, merge(AIM, { Torso: [8, -16, 2] })\n24:  { name: 'WalkHandsTied', frames: 24, loop: true, keys: [K(0, { Pelvis: { r: [4, 0, 0] }, LegR: [-22, 0, 0], ShinR: [8, 0, 0], LegL: [14, 0, 0], ShinL: [24, 0, 0], ArmR: [18, 8\n106:  { name: 'Run', frames: 14, loop: true, fast: true, keys: [K(0, { Body: { r: [-8, 0, 0], p: [0, 0.1, 0] }, Neck: [-8, 0, 0], LegFR: [-60, 0, 0], LegFL: [-44, 0, 0], LegBR: [54","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98060110-4ead-4574-964f-daef0a492581","uuid":"849cd6b6-120f-4c4b-875f-9911b87375a5","timestamp":"2026-11-06T09:02:27.957Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"**Patterns to follow:**\n- **One Game object, one Engine.** `createGame()` builds the world once. Title, attract, campaign and round are modes on it (`game.mode`). Don't use `engine.loadGame` between them: it would throw away the terrain. For New Game and Attract use `world.reset()`, \n- **Data over code.** All content lives in `src/content/` and `src/art/` as plain data. Adding a weapon, site, mission, line of dialogue or model must not need a code change. This is what lets the rest of the game be built later \"with normal designer tools\": t\n- **Actions, not keys.** `src/core/actions.js` maps an action to its pad code and its keyboard/mouse codes (section 16). All gameplay asks for actions. In `fixedUpdate` use `input.consumeAny(codes)`; in `update` use `wasPressed`.\n- **Gameplay in `fixedUpdate`, presentation in `update`.** All randomness comes from `ctx.random.fork(name)`, never `Math.random`. Cosmetic forks are made in `setup`.\n- **`TUNING`.** Every balance number lives in `src/content/tuning-defaults.js`, copied to a live `TUNING` object. Systems read `TUNING.x` at the moment of use and never cache it, so sliders act instantly.\n**Base:** the engine's native system. `ClipDef` data at 30 fps, `compileClips`, `THREE.AnimationMixer`, `gaitClip` for walks and runs, `Ragdoll`, `SpringChain`, `Squash`, `twoBoneIK`, tweens for small things, `Timeline` for scenes.\n\n**From `HERO_CLIPS`, reused on all people:** Idle, IdleLook, Walk, Run, Crouch, CrouchWalk, Crawl, Sit, SitDown, StandUp, LieIdle, Sleep, Hurt, HitReact, Death, Wave, Shout, Push, Climb. `analyzeClip` and `validateClip` check your own.\n\n**New, on the people rig** (`src/art/clips.js`):\n- **Upper-body, armed versions:** AimIdle, AimWalk (arms holding the rifle, played over the legs), FireRecoil, Reload, ThrowBottle.\n- **New whole-body clips:** BurnPanic (arms flailing, a stumbling run), Beg, Surrender, WoundedSit (clutching a side), DragBackward, CarryOver, DriveSit, UnjamSwear, WalkHandsTied, Shrug (Tibor), SmokeIdle (Odile), CleanRifleIdle (Vance), WriteAtDesk (Harrow), TeachPoint (Ansa).\n\n**To layer upper over lower,** split clips by filtering tracks: `new THREE.AnimationClip(name, clip.duration, clip.tracks.filter(t => /^(Pelvis|Leg|Shin|Foot)/.test(t.name)))`, and the rest for the upper body, then play one of each.\n\n**New, on the hands rig** (`src/art/viewmodels.js` + clips):\n- Idle sway and walk bob (procedural), ADS raise, fire kick per gun.\n- Reload per gun (magazine out and in on `Mag`, bolt on `Bolt`; revolver opens; shells for `mule`; flare breaks open).\n- **Unjam** (slap and rack), **falls apart**, equip and holster.\n- Cane knife swing, throw, plant, detonator click.\n- Tablet to mouth, syrette, **four surgery scenes**, **raise map** and tracker, monocular, wrench on bonnet, hand on wheel and shifter, finish-it.\n\n**Fauna:** gazelle run and graze on its own rig; vulture wing flap.\n\n=== function gaitClip\n3637:function gaitClip(rig: RigSpec, g: GaitSpec): ClipDef\n=== class SpringChain\n3795:### class SpringChain\n=== class Squash\n3817:### class Squash\n=== function twoBoneIK\n3836:function twoBoneIK(root: Vec3, target: Vec3, a: number, b: number, pole: Vec3, out: Vec3 = [0, 0, 0]): Vec3\n=== interface GaitClipOptions\\|interface GaitOptions\n=== interface SpringChainOptions\n3808:### interface SpringChainOptions\n=== interface SquashOptions\n### gaitClip()\n\n```ts\nfunction gaitClip(rig: RigSpec, g: GaitSpec): ClipDef\n```\n\n### gaitPartners()\n\n```ts\nfunction gaitPartners(n: number): number[][]\n```\n\nPartners for `n` legs in two rows (left 0, 2, 4…, right 1, 3, 5…): a leg waits for the legs beside and opposite it.\n\n### interface GaitSpec\n### class SpringChain\n\nA chain of points hanging off a moving root. Call `update(dt, root, basis)` every frame\nwith the root's world position and its orientation (three columns: right, up, forward),\nthen read `points` (root first).\n\n- `new SpringChain(o: SpringChainOptions)`\n- `readonly points: Vec3[]`\n- `o: Required<SpringChainOptions>`\n- `reset(root: Vec3, basis: readonly [Vec3, Vec3, Vec3]): void`: Put the chain straight out in its rest pose (no swing).\n- `update(dt: number, root: Vec3, basis: readonly [Vec3, Vec3, Vec3]): void`\n- `swing(basis: readonly [Vec3, Vec3, Vec3]): number`: How far the tip is from where the rest pose puts it (m): how much it is swinging.\n\n### interface SpringChainOptions\n\n### class Squash\n\nSquash and stretch as a damped spring on `value` (0 = rest, + stretched, − squashed).\n`scale()` turns it into a volume-preserving pair: `const [h, v] = squash.scale();\nmesh.scale.set(h, v, h)`.\n\n- `value: number`\n- `velocity: number`\n- `stiffness: number`: Spring stiffness and damping (a critically damped spring has damping = 2√stiffness).\n- `damping: number`\n- `amount: number`: 0 turns it off; 2.5 is rubbery.\n- `kick(v: number): void`: Add a kick: negative squashes (a landing), positive stretches (a jump).\n- `set(v: number): void`: Set the shape directly (a held squash).\n- `update(dt: number): void`\n- `scale(out: [number, number] = [1, 1]): [number, number]`: [horizontal, vertical] scale: y = 1 + s, xz = 1 / √(1 + s), so the volume stays put.\n### twoBoneIK()\n\n```ts\nfunction twoBoneIK(root: Vec3, target: Vec3, a: number, b: number, pole: Vec3, out: Vec3 = [0, 0, 0]): Vec3\n```\n\nWhere the middle joint of a two-bone limb goes (a knee, an elbow) so the end reaches\n`target` from `root` with bones `a` and `b` long, bending toward `pole` (a point the knee\npoints at). Analytic (the law of cosines), no iterations; a target out of reach straightens\nthe limb toward it, one too close folds it as far as it goes. Returns the joint, into `out`.\n\n### validateClip()\n\n```ts\nfunction validateClip(clip: ClipDef, rig: RigSpec): string[]\n352:const tail = new SpringChain({ segments: 6, length: 0.12 });   // tail.update(dt, root, [right, up, forward]); tail.points\n353:const squash = new Squash();                                   // squash.kick(-5); squash.update(dt); squash.scale() → [xz, y]\n355:legs.update(dt, body, yaw, velocity, (x, z) => 0);             // legs.feet[i].at; knee = twoBoneIK(hip, foot, a, b, pole)\n   59 src/actors/rig.js\n  113 src/art/clips.js\n  172 total\n// A person's view: model on the hero rig, shared compiled clips, layered upper and lower body, ragdoll on death.\nimport { buildModel, compileClips, HERO_CLIPS, HERO_RAGDOLL, HERO_RIG, Ragdoll, setLookLayer, THREE } from '../../pixel-engine.js';\nimport { CATALOG } from '../art/models.js';\nimport { PEOPLE_CLIPS } from '../art/clips.js';\nconst { AnimationClip, AnimationMixer, LoopOnce, LoopRepeat } = THREE;\nlet CLIPS = null, LOWER = null, UPPER = null;\nconst LEGS = /^(Pelvis|Leg|Shin|Foot)/;\nconst KEEP = ['Idle', 'IdleLook', 'Walk', 'Run', 'Crouch', 'CrouchWalk', 'Crawl', 'Sit', 'SitDown', 'StandUp', 'LieIdle', 'Sleep', 'Hurt', 'HitReact', 'Death', 'Wave', 'Shout', 'Push', 'Climb'];\nexport const RIG = { ...HERO_RIG, spine: undefined };\nfunction compile(object) {\n  if (CLIPS) return;\n  const defs = [...HERO_CLIPS.filter((c) => KEEP.includes(c.name)), ...PEOPLE_CLIPS];\n  const all = compileClips(defs, RIG, object);\n  CLIPS = {}; LOWER = {}; UPPER = {};\n  for (const c of all) {\n    CLIPS[c.name] = c;\n    LOWER[c.name] = new AnimationClip(`${c.name}:L`, c.duration, c.tracks.filter((t) => LEGS.test(t.name)));\n    UPPER[c.name] = new AnimationClip(`${c.name}:U`, c.duration, c.tracks.filter((t) => !LEGS.test(t.name)));\n  }\n}\nexport const clipNames = () => Object.keys(CLIPS ?? {});\nexport class PersonView {\n  constructor(ctx, modelId, palette, { gun = false } = {}) {\n    this.ctx = ctx;\n    const b = buildModel(modelId, { catalog: CATALOG, palette });\n    this.object = b.object;\n    compile(b.object);\n    setLookLayer(this.object, 'actors');\n    b.object.traverse((o) => { if (o.isMesh) { o.castShadow = true; o.frustumCulled = false; } });\n    ctx.scene.add(this.object);\n8:  { name: 'AimWalk', frames: 24, loop: true, keys: [K(0, merge(AIM, { Torso: [8, -16, 2] })), K(12, merge(AIM, { Torso: [8, -12, -2] })), K(24, merge(AIM, { Torso: [8, -16, 2] })\n24:  { name: 'WalkHandsTied', frames: 24, loop: true, keys: [K(0, { Pelvis: { r: [4, 0, 0] }, LegR: [-22, 0, 0], ShinR: [8, 0, 0], LegL: [14, 0, 0], ShinL: [24, 0, 0], ArmR: [18, 8\n106:  { name: 'Run', frames: 14, loop: true, fast: true, keys: [K(0, { Body: { r: [-8, 0, 0], p: [0, 0.1, 0] }, Neck: [-8, 0, 0], LegFR: [-60, 0, 0], LegFL: [-44, 0, 0], LegBR: [54","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Rh5KWWz13MsVmdFo3Mufos","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
