{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K1GqY7Rvzyvmc2Mgtr9dL7","type":"tool_result","content":"build 2c1ef0d002d3\n2531 passed, 0 failed, 0 suites unchanged\nafter 2c1ef0d002d3\n317\n16\nsheet-tmp.png\n\n[exited with code 0]\njson ok 43 logged 18.\n**The fire grid** is the game's signature system, so write it first and test it hardest.\n\n- 256 × 256 cells at 5 m (`src/world/fire.js`). Arrays: `fuel` (0 none, 1 grass, 2 scrub, 3 tree, 4 building), `state` (0 fresh, 1 burning, 2 burnt, 3 regrowing), `burnEnd` and `burntAt`. Road, water,\n- Tick at 4 Hz in `fixedUpdate` (every 15 steps), using `ctx.random.fork('fire')`. Keep a list of burning cells; never scan the grid.\n- Each burning cell tries its 8 neighbours with `p = 0.02 * fuelFactor * windFactor * slopeFactor * rainFactor * TUNING.fireSpread`, divided by 1.41 for diagonals. I calibrated 0.02 by simulating this\n  - `windFactor = clamp(1 + TUNING.windEffect * windSpeed/5 * 1.6 * cos(angle between neighbour direction and wind), 0.15, 3.5)`\n  - `slopeFactor` = 1.4 uphill, 0.7 downhill. `rainFactor` = 0.15 while raining. `fuelFactor`: grass 1, scrub 0.8, tree 0.6, building 0.4.\n- Strong wind (above 6 m/s) gives an ember jump: small chance to light a fuel cell 2 to 3 cells downwind, which is how fire crosses a road.\n- Burn time: grass 8 to 14 s, scrub 12 to 18 s, tree and building 30 to 40 s.\n- **A test must measure the head of the fire at wind 5 m/s and require 2 to 5 m/s,** with flanks clearly slower, so a sprinting or running player can escape and a walking one (3.6 m/s) struggles.\n- **Burnt land can't burn again.** That is mechanics and plot at once.\n- `ignite(x, z, radius)` is the only way in. Used by flare, molotov, flamethrower, explosions, burning soldiers, wrecks and tracer fire on full-auto from the mounted MG (small chance).\n- `burnStrip(polylineId, width)` quietly burns a named strip, for story scars (section 14).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98060110-4ead-4574-964f-daef0a492581","uuid":"6b78456a-eac1-4aed-976e-642c4c6bd42c","timestamp":"2026-11-06T11:47:03.525Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"build 2c1ef0d002d3\n2531 passed, 0 failed, 0 suites unchanged\nafter 2c1ef0d002d3\n317\n16\nsheet-tmp.png\n\n[exited with code 0]\njson ok 43 logged 18.\n**The fire grid** is the game's signature system, so write it first and test it hardest.\n\n- 256 × 256 cells at 5 m (`src/world/fire.js`). Arrays: `fuel` (0 none, 1 grass, 2 scrub, 3 tree, 4 building), `state` (0 fresh, 1 burning, 2 burnt, 3 regrowing), `burnEnd` and `burntAt`. Road, water,\n- Tick at 4 Hz in `fixedUpdate` (every 15 steps), using `ctx.random.fork('fire')`. Keep a list of burning cells; never scan the grid.\n- Each burning cell tries its 8 neighbours with `p = 0.02 * fuelFactor * windFactor * slopeFactor * rainFactor * TUNING.fireSpread`, divided by 1.41 for diagonals. I calibrated 0.02 by simulating this\n  - `windFactor = clamp(1 + TUNING.windEffect * windSpeed/5 * 1.6 * cos(angle between neighbour direction and wind), 0.15, 3.5)`\n  - `slopeFactor` = 1.4 uphill, 0.7 downhill. `rainFactor` = 0.15 while raining. `fuelFactor`: grass 1, scrub 0.8, tree 0.6, building 0.4.\n- Strong wind (above 6 m/s) gives an ember jump: small chance to light a fuel cell 2 to 3 cells downwind, which is how fire crosses a road.\n- Burn time: grass 8 to 14 s, scrub 12 to 18 s, tree and building 30 to 40 s.\n- **A test must measure the head of the fire at wind 5 m/s and require 2 to 5 m/s,** with flanks clearly slower, so a sprinting or running player can escape and a walking one (3.6 m/s) struggles.\n- **Burnt land can't burn again.** That is mechanics and plot at once.\n- `ignite(x, z, radius)` is the only way in. Used by flare, molotov, flamethrower, explosions, burning soldiers, wrecks and tracer fire on full-auto from the mounted MG (small chance).\n- `burnStrip(polylineId, width)` quietly burns a named strip, for story scars (section 14).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01K1GqY7Rvzyvmc2Mgtr9dL7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
