{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgmieLvsxSMZME3HU1eiE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019naJ5CYLX7f567cf5kjPDg","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162030__x07393c/work/PLAN.md","offset":580,"limit":300,"allow_large":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12796,"cache_read_input_tokens":377133,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12796},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98060110-4ead-4574-964f-daef0a492581","uuid":"73defec6-5f65-47f2-9758-b62337b121ec","timestamp":"2026-11-06T13:02:30.131Z","request_id":"req_011CgmieLcHAe72857cyVgRJ","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_019naJ5CYLX7f567cf5kjPDg":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162030__x07393c/work/PLAN.md","offset":580,"limit":300,"allow_large":true}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019naJ5CYLX7f567cf5kjPDg","type":"tool_result","content":"580\t- Men you were paid to kill\n581\t- Friends lost\n582\t- Stones earned\n583\t\n584\tWritten as Harrow would write it.\n585\t\n586\t**Saving:** single slot, versioned JSON in `localStorage` (`src/core/save.js`), written on sleep and on mission complete, read through `ctx.input.send` so replays stay exact. Main menu's Continue loads it. Dev mode has Quick Save/Load.\n587\t\n588\t---\n589\t\n590\t## 14. Missions\n591\t\n592\t**Format** (`src/content/missions.js`), a sketch:\n593\t```js\n594\t{ id:'m3', title:'FUEL FOR THE PEACE', giver:'vance', requires:['m2'], pay:15, wind:{ dir:[-0.8,-0.6], speed:5 },\n595\t  brief:['vance:m3.brief.1','vance:m3.brief.2'],\n596\t  alt:{ buddy:'ines', call:'ines:m3.alt', bonus:5, steps:[ {do:'steal',tag:'tanker',text:'TAKE THE TANKER AT P3'} ] },\n597\t  steps:[ {do:'goto',site:'east-siding',r:140,text:'REACH THE SIDING'},\n598\t          {do:'destroy',tag:'fuel-tank',n:3,text:'BURN THE TANKS'},\n599\t          {do:'leave',site:'east-siding',r:220,text:'GET OUT'},\n600\t          {do:'report',to:'vance',text:'REPORT TO VANCE'} ],\n601\t  onDone:[ {burnStrip:'A'}, {ledger:{paid:15}} ] }\n602\t```\n603\t**Step types:** `goto leave talk report use deliver destroy kill collect steal hold escort ride timer choice script`. A step shows its `text` for 5 s at the top when it starts, and always in the map margin. Bots drive these same steps.\n604\t\n605\tContracts are taken in person (a short FP scene: the camera holds on the giver, subtitles, then Accept or Not Yet) or through the notice board in Mile Forty. After M2, the order within M3/M4 and M5/M6 is free; M5 needs M3 and M6 needs M4 (one faction's path each); M7 needs all four. Acts, for the fever's pace: act 1 is M0 to M2, act 2 is M3 to M6, act 3 is M7 onward.\n606\t\n607\t| # | Title (giver) | Length, time | What happens | Teaches | Alternate plan | Consequence, pay |\n608\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n609\t| M0 | The Goods Line | 2 min, dusk, skippable | You ride Old Bakr's flatcar into the Kettle as he talks. Prompt: raise the map (must do). The margin note. Fever on the platform; you fall | Look, map | - | Fade to the clinic |\n610\t| M1 | Mercy Run (Odile) | 7 min, morning | Wake at the clinic. Take a tablet. Given an old `tractor` (cond 45). Drive medicine to Three Wells. On the way back P2 is manned. The 5th shot **jams by script**; then the truck is hit and stalls: repair. Syrette. Report | Walk, use, tablet, drive, waypoint, fire, jam, reload, syrette, repair | - | +3 tablets, 5 stones, Pump Shed |\n611\t| M2 | A Cage at the Post (Tibor) | 7 min, best at night | Ines owes Tibor. She's in a cage at Ranger Post (8 Concord, a tower). Scout with the monocular, cross in grass, cane knife, or go loud. Open the cage (hold). Ines fights her way out with you. She explains rescues by doing one if you fall | Monocular, stealth, melee, sleep to choose the hour, safehouse capture, buddy | - | Ranger Post safehouse, 8 stones, Ines |\n612\t| M3 | Fuel for the Peace (Vance) | 7 min | Burn the Harvest's 3 tanks at East Siding. Vance hands you the flare pistol. Wind pinned toward the depot: the grass will carry fire if you start it upwind | Flare, wind, fire, chain explosions | Ines: steal the tanker at P3 and drive it in; soldiers hold fire until you're inside | Scar A, 15 stones (+5). A column of smoke visible across the map for a game day |\n613\t| M4 | Seed Money (Ansa) | 7 min | Payroll convoy (2 technicals, a truck) crosses the Salt Pan on a loop. Stop it, take the case. It flies out when the truck blows: you get the tracker to find it in the salt | Vehicle combat, MG, tracker | Dov: plant his charges on the bridge, detonate as the convoy crosses | 20 stones (+5), tracker, Dov |\n614\t| M5 | The Water Question (Vance) | 7 min | Destroy the pump on the Mercy, because Three Wells \"feeds the Harvest\" | Charges, defending, moral cost | Mags: first open the bypass and hold the pump house for 60 s, so the cistern fills | Without alt: Three Wells empties, a line of people walks the road to the clinic, its huts go dark, Odile refuses tablets until you do a Mercy Run free. With alt: village stays, pay 10 instead of 20 |\n615\t| M6 | The Long Field (Ansa) | 9 min, forced night | Burn the Concord's crop and its ammo bunker. Your highest-trust buddy comes along (with no buddy alive, a Harvest guide named Pell does). At about 70% the wind turns (scripted) and they go down on fire: **Syrette or Finish It** | Night fire, buddy choice | The mission itself | Scar B, 25 stones, the Ledger's first hard line |\n616\t| M7 | The Cut (Harrow's note) | 10 min | A note at your safehouse: *You have drawn well. Come and see.* Truce collapses: both armies fight for the mine. Reach the sluice house through crossfire and wildfire, take his ledger. In it: *One contractor, paid in advance, to walk the Kettle.* Signed by him | Three-way fight, technical MG, big fire | A surviving buddy calls: they hold the east road if you go in from the pit side (no bonus stones, +1 trust) | Scar C. Truce over: Mile Forty loses its no-fire zone, Tibor moves his stock into safehouse lockers. Act 2 fever pace |\n617\t| M8 | Last Train (Odile) | 7 min | Mile Forty under shells. Hold the platform 120 s while people board. Then ride Old Bakr's train to East Siding on a flatcar MG, 60 s, on rails, under fire. *He says the grass won't burn twice.* The column starts walking the scar | Defence, on-rails MG | - | Column on the map, moving slowly and visibly along the scar |\n618\t| M9 | The Surveyor | 10 min, night, storm | Climb to the Observatory (deserters from both armies; no fires, it's raining). Harrow sits at a table with a lamp, as sick as you. The scene: he lays your contract map down; the three scars glow as one line; he draws the last stroke. He offers tablets and the minefield sheet, and asks you to finish your contract, or not | Choice | - | `choice` steps: shoot him or don't (a Ledger line, no other effect). Then who gets the sheet |\n619\t| End | The Pass | 3 to 4 min | Either walk to the Pass alone, or take the sheet to the column and hold behind them. Surviving buddies arrive (200 HP, real AI, last lines), with pursuit from both armies. Rain stops. The last grass is yours to light | Everything | - | Ending card, Ledger, credits, title. Continue returns to the last safehouse for free roam |\n620\t\n621\t**Story scars.** On completing M3, M6 and M7, call `burnStrip('A'|'B'|'C')` so the arc exists whatever the player actually burned: A from East Siding west to the Cut, C across the Cut, B from the Cut west through the Long Field to the Pass road. The player sees it first in M9.\n622\t\n623\t**Ending cards:**\n624\t- **Walk out:** *You reached the border with a case of stones and a map nobody else will ever use. The guard asks your trade. You tell him: surveyor.*\n625\t- **Give it to them:** *They crossed at first light, walking on ash. Nobody has asked who lit it. The fever is not finished with you, and you are out of tablets. It is a good view.*\n626\t\n627\t**Attract, tests and dev mode** can jump to any mission start: each mission has a `setup` that puts the world in the right state (`world.reset`, story flags, scars, buddies, loadout), so `dev.startMission('m6')` is one call.\n628\t\n629\t---\n630\t\n631\t## 15. Writing\n632\t\n633\t**Voice.** Weary, literary and exact. Short declarative sentences. Euphemism as cruelty. Gallows humour without a wink. Nobody explains the theme. Nobody is your friend without a price. People are tired, and they're smart. Think of a war correspondent who stopped filing years ago. Don't quote real authors, and don't imitate the source's lines.\n634\t\n635\tEach mission gets 8 to 15 spoken lines in this voice. Each character has a tic: **Vance** invoices (*conclude, regrettable, the matter of*). **Ansa** corrects grammar. **Odile** counts things. **Tibor** talks about returns. **Bakr** tells you what stations used to be called. **Ines** owes people, or they owe her. **Dov** tells a three-sentence story that ends badly. **Mags** narrates what she is doing to you. **Harrow** writes like a surveyor's notebook.\n636\t\n637\tAll game text must be in the HUD font's character set. Subtitle lines stay under 60 characters, two lines at most: split long sentences across lines in sequence.\n638\t\n639\tUse these lines verbatim, and write the rest to match:\n640\t\n641\t- **Bakr, M0:** *Forty miles of track and not one station that remembers its name.* / *They paint the signs over. Whoever won last.* / *You have the look of a man who read about this place. Reading is a good way to visit.* / *Up there they will ask you which side. Say yes.*\n642\t- **Odile:** *Three tablets. The fourth you pay for. I do not mean in stones.* / *I do not need you to be good. I need you to be on time.* / *Sixty-one beds. Forty blankets. You are the math.*\n643\t- **Vance:** *We do not burn villages. We conclude them.* / *The water question has been a great sorrow to this office.* / *Your invoice will be honoured, regrettably.*\n644\t- **Ansa:** *You said less people. Fewer. Fewer people. It will matter by the end of the month.* / *Burn the field. A hungry man learns to read the wind.*\n645\t- **Tibor:** *Everything on this rack has been returned at least once.* / *It fires. If you want it to fire twice, that is a different price.*\n646\t- **Ines:** *I flew for both of them. Neither paid. Get in.* / *You owe me a truck. You owe me several trucks.*\n647\t- **Dov:** *Two fingers I left in this country. I came back to see what they are doing.* / *A man asked me to mine his own road, so he would know where it was safe. He was right for a week.*\n648\t- **Mags:** *Hold still. No, you can't feel that. No, that's normal. Hold still.* / *Not today. Today you owe me money.*\n649\t- **A burning buddy:** *Don't let it be the fire. Please. Not the fire.*\n650\t- **Barks:** *There! In the grass!* / *Who lit that?* / *It's stuck! It's stuck again!* / *Leave him, he's already gone.*\n651\t- **Harrow's margin notes,** one per trig point, in order:\n652\t  1. *A map is a promise made by someone who has already left.*\n653\t  2. *I drew the river where the Company wanted it. The river was slow to comply, but it came round.*\n654\t  3. *Both armies buy from me. The Concord pays on time. The Harvest pays in grain and tears. I have eaten better on the tears.*\n655\t  4. *You will have noticed that you follow roads. I drew those too.*\n656\t  5. *Grass is the only honest border. It goes where the wind tells it, and it keeps a record.*\n657\t  6. *By now you have burned what I marked. Look at it from the ridge. Tell me that is not a line.*\n658\t- **Harrow, M9:** *You are late. I said you would be. Sit down, it won't take long, neither of us has long.* / *I drew the lines that started this. I would like to draw one more.* / *You have been drawing for me. Look at it.* / *Burned grass cannot burn twice. It is the only safe road in the country, and you built it for wages.*\n659\t- **Load-screen epigraphs** (*from Harrow's field notes*): write 12 in the same voice.\n660\t\n661\t---\n662\t\n663\t## 16. UI and UX\n664\t\n665\t**10-foot and controller first.** A PS5 DualSense on a TV at ten feet is the design target. Mouse and keyboard play the same game on the same screens and feel native. Everything is drawn with `ctx.hud` in art pixels; there is no DOM UI at all, so it all works in Node tests. Test the view at 1920×1080.\n666\t\n667\t**Layout rules:**\n668\t- Safe area 24 px horizontal, 14 px vertical.\n669\t- Menu items at scale 2; the smallest text anywhere is scale 1 (subtitles, prompts).\n670\t- At most 6 items on a screen, one idea per screen.\n671\t- No tables, no scroll lists, no web-style data screens. Long content is paged.\n672\t- A focused item has a full-width bar in `orange` and a small marker. Move and confirm sounds.\n673\t- Only the title and pause menus cover the view. Every other screen is in your hands or an overlay with the world visible behind it.\n674\t\n675\t**HUD in play is minimal** and hides 6 s after it last changed:\n676\t- 5 health segments, syrette and tablet counts bottom-left.\n677\t- Ammo and the gun's condition icon bottom-right.\n678\t- A dot reticle (hidden while scoped; the scope has its own black mask).\n679\t- Prompts centre-bottom. Subtitles above them with the speaker's name in a colour.\n680\t- Mission step at the top for 5 s when it changes.\n681\t\n682\t**Controls** (`src/core/actions.js`):\n683\t\n684\t| Action | DualSense | Xbox glyph | Keyboard and mouse |\n685\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n686\t| Move / look | L stick / R stick | same | WASD / mouse |\n687\t| Fire / aim | R2 / L2 | RT / LT | LMB / RMB |\n688\t| Use (when a prompt shows), else reload | Square | X | E / R |\n689\t| Jump | Cross | A | Space |\n690\t| Crouch | Circle | B | C (never Ctrl: Ctrl+W closes the browser tab) |\n691\t| Sprint | L3 (click) | LS | Left Shift |\n692\t| Melee | R3 | RS | F |\n693\t| Next weapon | Triangle | Y | Wheel, or 1-4 |\n694\t| Throw / plant | R1 | RB | G |\n695\t| Syrette, surgery | L1 | LB | Q |\n696\t| Map up / down | D-pad Up | D-pad Up | M or Tab |\n697\t| Tablet | D-pad Down | D-pad Down | H |\n698\t| Tracker | D-pad Left | D-pad Left | T |\n699\t| Monocular (hold) | D-pad Right | D-pad Right | V |\n700\t| Pause | Options | Menu | Esc |\n701\t| Ledger | Create | View | J |\n702\t| **Driving:** gas / brake-reverse / steer | R2 / L2 / L stick | RT / LT / L stick | W / S / A-D |\n703\t| Handbrake | Cross | A | Space |\n704\t| Get out / repair | Square | X | E |\n705\t| Swap to gun | Triangle | Y | F |\n706\t| Chase camera | R3 | RS | C |\n707\t\n708\tUse `input.preventKeys.add('Tab')` etc. Analog triggers: each frame, read `navigator.getGamepads()` buttons 6 and 7 `value` and `input.send({ tr:[l2, r2] })` when changed, so recordings keep it, and use it for throttle and brake. Rumble: `pad.vibrationActuator?.playEffect('dual-rumble', {...})`, guarded, Settings toggle.\n709\t\n710\t**Glyphs.** Prompts follow the input used last:\n711\t- `device` flips to `kbm` on keydown, mouse button or real mouse movement, and to `pad` on any `Pad*` code or a stick past 0.35.\n712\t- `src/ui/glyphs.js` is pixel art as `hud.sprite` rows, about 11 × 11: Cross, Circle, Square, Triangle, L1, L2, R1, R2, L3, R3, D-pad directions, Options, Create; Xbox A, B, X, Y, LB, LT, RB, RT, LS, RS, Menu, View; a key cap drawn around any letter; LMB, RMB, MMB, wheel.\n713\t- Settings has **Glyphs: PlayStation / Xbox**, default PlayStation.\n714\t- `game.state().prompts` lists what's on screen, so tests can check it.\n715\t\n716\t**The mouse is native.** In menus the pointer is free (no lock), hover moves focus, click activates (read `input.buttonEvents`; convert with `x = (p.x+1)/2*hud.width`, `y = (1-p.y)/2*hud.height`). The wheel scrolls pages. Over the world it aims and looks under pointer lock. On the held map it's a cursor (hover focuses a marker, click sets the waypoint). On Tibor's rack and in dialogue choices, click works too. Keyboard in menus: arrows or WASD, Enter or Space, Esc back. Pad in menus: D-pad or left stick with key repeat, Cross confirms, Circle goes back, L1/R1 change tabs and pages. If the pad disconnects during play, open the pause menu.\n717\t\n718\t**The held map** (`src/world/map-texture.js`). The heart of pillar 3.\n719\t- 320 × 240 DataTexture on a plane about 0.5 × 0.375 m, about 0.42 m in front of the camera, tilted, in both hands (the `hand` model and hands rig), filling about 70% of the width, so one texel is about one art pixel. A 0.62 m plane, which I tried first, was too big.\n720\t- Baked at start: contour lines every 8 m on sand paper, river, roads, rail, labels in your own 5×7 `pixfont.js`.\n721\t- Redrawn at up to 2 Hz on a copy: burn scars (ink), your position and heading, the waypoint, sites you've seen, mission step and Harrow's notes in the margin, wind arrow and clock on a small GPS clipped to the corner.\n722\t- Raise and lower takes 0.4 s with paper sound. **The world never stops.** You can walk and drive with it up. While it's up, the look input moves the map cursor.\n723\t- Square/LMB on a marker sets the waypoint; Triangle or wheel toggles a closer zoom.\n724\t- It works at night because the paper uses a dim lit toon plus a small hand torch `lights.request` following the view group.\n725\t\n726\t**Screens:**\n727\t- **Loading:** the engine's, then a black screen with one Harrow epigraph.\n728\t- **Title:** live 3D scene (dusk, fixed slow camera over burning grass on the Long Field, music), the title large (scale 4, or 3 if it won't fit), the latest input's *Press [glyph]*. Then the main menu.\n729\t- **Main menu:** Continue (when a save exists), New Game, Cash Run, Settings, About and Credits.\n730\t- **Pause** (`timeScale = 0`): Resume, Ledger, Settings, Dev Mode, About and Credits, Quit to Title. In a hub session: Resume and Settings only.\n731\t- **Settings:** Sound (Music slider **default 10%**, Effects, Voices), Controls (Look sensitivity for pad, for mouse; Invert Y; Aim assist; Rumble; Glyphs), Picture (Fullscreen, for the TV; Pixel size Fine/Chunky via `engine.settings.set`; Quality; Field of view), Comfort (Subtitle size; Reduce flashes; Fever effects reduced), Reset to Defaults. Saved in your own `localStorage` entry and re-applied at boot: `settings:{ button:false, key:false }` hides the engine's panel and stops the engine saving its own copy.\n732\t- **Dialogue:** the camera holds on the speaker; subtitles; two big buttons at most.\n733\t- **Tibor's rack:** one gun at a time, large (its first-person model turned to the side on a table), name, three bars (Damage, Range, Reliability), price. Left/right cycles. Buy or Take.\n734\t- **Locker:** one row per slot, left/right picks.\n735\t- **Bed:** Dawn, Noon, Dusk, Midnight, Leave.\n736\t- **Ledger:** section 13.\n737\t- **Game Over, Ending card, Credits.**\n738\t- **About and Credits:** paged, see section 27.\n739\t\n740\t**Touch-only devices.** Detect with `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches` and no pad connected (verified: true on Chromium with the `iPhone 14`, `iPad Pro 11` and `Pixel 7` profiles, false on a desktop context). Engine option `touch:false` always, so there are never on-screen controls. On such a device the title shows **Controller or keyboard required** (the exact text in `state().notice`, drawn uppercase by the font) and one large **Settings** button (tap works as click: `input.buttonEvents` reports a finger as code `Touch`). Attract mode still starts after 10 s; a tap exits to this screen. A key press or pad connecting clears the gate and shows the normal title.\n741\t\n742\t---\n743\t\n744\t## 17. Dev mode\n745\t\n746\tPause menu → **Dev Mode** (hidden in a hub session). An overlay with tabs (L1/R1 or Q/E), world visible behind, playing or frozen by a toggle.\n747\t\n748\t| Tab | Contents |\n749\t| --- | --- |\n750\t| Cheats | God mode, infinite ammo, no jams, no fever, invisible to AI, noclip fly |\n751\t| Teleport | Every site, every post, every case, the crosshair point |\n752\t| Spawn | Squad of each faction, pickup, technical, truck, a stone case, a buddy |\n753\t| World | Hour slider, wind direction and speed sliders, weather (clear, dust, storm), ignite at crosshair, extinguish all, regrow all, sleep +6 h |\n754\t| Mission | Start any mission, complete current step, set story flags, give stones, tablets, syrettes, all guns; break gun; force jam; force fever; down a buddy |\n755\t| **Balance** | Live sliders (below), **Reset to Defaults** for all, Square/R resets one |\n756\t| Debug | Fire-grid overlay, nav overlay, AI state text over heads, counts (actors, burning cells, draw info from `engine.state()`), engine debug panel (`engine.showDebug`), free camera (`engine.setCamera({ preset:'free' })`, restored after; re-install `step` in `onCameraChange`), crosshair coordinates for placing things in `src/content/`, Quick Save/Load, show `status()` |\n757\t\n758\t**Balance sliders** (left/right steps, hold accelerates, mouse drags). Defaults in `src/content/tuning-defaults.js`:\n759\t\n760\t| Slider | Default | Range |\n761\t| --- | --- | --- |\n762\t| `playerSpeed` multiplier | 1 | 0.5-2 |\n763\t| `playerDamageTaken` multiplier | 1 | 0-3 |\n764\t| `weaponDamage` multiplier | 1 | 0.25-4 |\n765\t| `enemyHealth` multiplier | 1 | 0.25-4 |\n766\t| `enemyAccuracy` | 1 | 0.25-3 |\n767\t| `enemyVision` (m) | 90 | 20-200 |\n768\t| `enemyReaction` (s) | 0.45 | 0.1-2 |\n769\t| `wearRate` | 1 | 0-5 |\n770\t| `jamRate` | 1 | 0-5 |\n771\t| `fireSpread` | 1 | 0-3 |\n772\t| `fireDamage` (HP/s) | 8 | 0-30 |\n773\t| `windEffect` | 1 | 0-3 |\n774\t| `feverMinutes` | 12 | 2-40 |\n775\t| `vehicleTopSpeed` (m/s) | 26 | 10-45 |\n776\t| `vehicleToughness` | 1 | 0.25-4 |\n777\t| `stonesReward` multiplier | 1 | 0-5 |\n778\t| `buddyWoundChance` | 0.15 | 0-1 |\n779\t| `dayMinutes` | 30 | 2-120 |\n780\t| `postRemanHours` | 24 | 1-96 |\n781\t| `regrowHours` | 48 | 1-200 |\n782\t\n783\tA test sets every slider, checks the system responds, presses Reset, and checks every value equals its default.\n784\t\n785\t---\n786\t\n787\t## 18. Attract mode\n788\t\n789\tAfter **10 seconds with no input on the title screen or main menu**, start a looping demo (`src/attract/`). Settings and About are exempt, because people stop to read them. It's a director with a list of beats, using the real game with `cam.override`, god mode, infinite ammo and bot input through the same action layer. It cheats freely: teleports, spawns, sets the hour and wind. A `save.disabled` flag stops it touching saves.\n790\t\n791\tBeats (10 to 14 s each, joined by `engine.screen.cover('dither')` and `reveal`), to show as much as possible:\n792\t1. Dusk, driving a technical down the road, first person, raising the map at the wheel.\n793\t2. Rolling into a checkpoint, gunfight, the gun jams, slap and rack.\n794\t3. Flare into dry grass, the wind takes it, soldiers run burning.\n795\t4. Night, the Long Field in flames, chase camera past it.\n796\t5. Fever: the view swims, tablet to mouth.\n797\t6. Field surgery with pliers.\n798\t7. Scoped shot from a ridge at noon.\n799\t8. Dragged out by a buddy; syrette or finish it.\n800\t9. Tracker beeping to a case in a burnt wreck.\n801\t10. Train with the flatcar MG.\n802\t11. Tibor's rack, a line of his.\n803\t12. The map on a table with the scars glowing.\n804\t13. The title.\n805\t\n806\tHUD shows a `DEMO` tag and *Press [glyph]*. **Any input exits** (key, mouse button or real movement, pad button or stick, tap) back to the screen it came from, after `world.reset()`. The loop must run indefinitely without error. It runs behind the touch gate too. Never in a hub session.\n807\t\n808\t---\n809\t\n810\t## 19. Multiplayer\n811\t\n812\tFollow the AI Hub Session Protocol v1 (read `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`; also the shared-world example `examples/arena.html` beside it). The hub runs invites, lobby, names, clock and results; the game runs the round. The same code also plays when the game is on its own.\n813\t\n814\t**Mode: `shared-world`, 1 to 4 players.** Four mercs in one burning valley, friends until the stones are counted.\n815\t\n816\t**The round, \"Cash Run\" (6 minutes):**\n817\t- The valley around the Cut: the campaign's terrain, with only the Cut, P5 and the Ranger Post live, 16 to 24 soldiers, wind and fire on.\n818\t- Six stone cases in guarded spots, shown by the tracker's beep and a marker when close. One extraction truck on the road south of the pit.\n819\t- Everyone starts at a different road end with `tractor` (cond 70), `flare`, `cane`, 2 syrettes, 2 bottles.\n820\t- Carry one case at a time (speed × 0.85, you can't sprint); walk it to the truck to bank its stones. Most stones wins.\n821\t- Down at 0 HP: you drop the case and bleed for 25 s. Another player can hold Use for 3 s to bring you up (+1 Revive) or just take the case. Bleed out and you return at your road end after 15 s. Friendly fire is on: that's the theme.\n822\t- On foot only, in rounds: no player vehicles.\n823\t- Ends when the time is up, or when all cases are banked or burned. Standings by stones, ties together.\n824\t\n825\t**Session head tags** go in the template (section 23): `hub:session` 1, `hub:session-players` `1-4`, `hub:session-mode` `shared-world`, `hub:session-minutes` `6`, `hub:webgpu` `required`, `hub:session-goal` *Carry the most diamond cases out of the burning mine*, `hub:session-howto` *Stick/WASD move, R2/mouse fire, Square/E use, carry cases to the truck*.\n826\t\n827\t**Boot order** (`src/main.js`). This is the part that makes the hub work:\n828\t```js\n829\tconst info = (window.AIHub && AIHub.active) ? await AIHub.connect({ mode:'shared-world', seats:[1,4], card:true }) : null;\n830\tif (info) {\n831\t  const game = createGame({ session: hubSession(info) });        // mode 'round': no title, no menus, no attract\n832\t  if (info.server) { const e = await Engine.headless(game, {}); AIHub.ready(); setInterval(() => e.step(6, 1/60), 100); }\n833\t  else if (!navigator.gpu) AIHub.fail('This game needs WebGPU');\n834\t  else await Engine.start(game, { ...OPTIONS, seed: info.seed });  // game.ready(ctx) calls AIHub.ready() once, with no key press\n835\t} else { /* normal start: touch check, title */ }\n836\t```\n837\tHandle a rejected `__PIXEL_READY__` by `AIHub.fail(message)`. If `connect` answers `null`, run as on your own.\n838\t\n839\t**`src/net/session.js`:** one interface, three implementations, so round code never knows which: `{ kind, me, players:[{id,name,color}], host, isHost, server, time(), rng(label), send(data,{to,reliable}), on(event,fn), ready(), answer(what), finish(outcome), fail(msg) }`.\n840\t- `hubSession` wraps `AIHub`.\n841\t- `soloSession` is **on its own**: host is you, the other seats are AI mercs (reuse the buddy brain: go to the nearest case, bank it, shoot what shoots you), with your own results screen at the end.\n842\t- `linkSession` is **on its own with a friend on the same computer**: `BroadcastChannel('game-link-v1')` between two windows. Host and Join on the Cash Run menu, a simple lobby, `start` carrying a `Date.now()` time base and a seed. It costs little, reuses everything, and is how two-window play gets tested.\n843\t\n844\tThe main menu's Cash Run offers: Solo with Hired Guns, Host on This Computer, Join on This Computer, plus one line saying friends online play through AI Hub.\n845\t\n846\t**Netcode.** The host runs the world. Each copy moves its own player from its own stick, at once, never waiting for the network, as `arena.html` does.\n847\t\n848\t| Message | Direction | Rate, kind | Content |\n849\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n850\t| `me` | client → host | 12/s, unreliable | seq, position, yaw, pitch, stance, weapon, hp echo |\n851\t| `ev` | client → host | up to 5/s, reliable, batched | shots since last batch (origin, dir, weapon), use, pick up, bank, revive, ignite |\n852\t| `s` | host → all | 10/s, unreliable, under 1,100 bytes | time, players, soldiers (`[id,x,z,yaw,state,hp]`, ints, y from terrain), cases |\n853\t| `w` | host → all | up to 4/s, reliable, batched | fire cells ignited and burnt, damage per player, downs, deaths, explosions, banks, sounds |\n854\t\n855\tThat's at most 17 messages a second per copy; the limit is 20 with bursts of 40, and 16 KB per message. **Drive sends from `setInterval`, not the render loop:** on a software-rendered copy `update` runs about twice a second, and traffic must still flow.\n856\t\n857\tClients render soldiers as puppets interpolated 150 ms behind; they run fire visuals only; health is host-authoritative. Local shots show muzzle flash and tracers at once, and the host decides hits. Older snapshots are dropped by `at`. In a shared world use `AIHub.rng(label)`, because `Math.random` isn't seeded there; the world is the same static terrain on all copies anyway.\n858\t\n859\t**The server case.** `AIHub.server` true: run the same host code under `Engine.headless` with no player, camera, audio or HUD (`me` isn't in `players`). Don't touch `info.players[me]`.\n860\t\n861\t**Round rules the harness checks:**\n862\t- `time-up`: the host calls `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, stats, awards })` **directly from the event handler**, within `graceMs` (5 s). Every present player appears once.\n863\t- `leave`: continue; the host finishes if nobody is left.\n864\t- `end`: no more input or sends, `audio.stopMusic()`, `audio.stopLoops()`, mute. The hub shows results.\n865\t- `stats` at most 6 names per player (Stones, Downs, Revives, Kills); `awards` up to 3 (*Last Friend* for most revives, *Paid in Full* for most stones, *Arsonist* for most cells lit).\n866\t\n867\t**In a session:** no title, menus or prompts before the round. No dialogs (`alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`), no `window.open`, no navigation, no network except the hub. Quit does nothing. Names come only from the hub (sanitize to the font's characters; HUD canvas, never HTML). No chat, emotes or custom names. **On a pad, ignore Options while Create is held** (Create + Options is the hub's). Sessions get an empty storage, so settings start at defaults, music at 10%.\n868\t\n869\t**The game's own card** (`card:true`). A shared-world card on your live scene with `GAME_TITLE`, the players in their seat colours with ready marks, how to win, this player's controls in their glyphs, time left from the `card` event. Ready: Enter, Cross, or a tap/click on Ready → `AIHub.answer('ready')`. More time: Triangle, key `M`, or tap → `AIHub.answer('more')`. It has no menus, and play begins only at `start`.\n870\t**Listen for Enter and M with a plain `window` keydown listener** (verified to pass the harness's card check), because the harness expects an answer within 3 s and the render loop may be slow. Pad buttons can poll in `update`. Everything on the card uses `AIHub.rng('card')` for randomness. When `AIHub.time() >= 0` the round is on; show the 3-2-1 countdown before that.\n871\t\n872\t**Fallback.** If shared-world can't be made stable, ship `ghost` (each copy its own world, others' mercs shown, `progress` and `result` by score, `Math.random` seeded for you) rather than drop multiplayer, and last of all `parallel`.\n873\t\n874\t**Test it:** section 24, all four harness scenarios, and two windows on `linkSession`, plus the game outside a session.\n875\t\n876\t---\n877\t\n878\t## 20. Art\n879\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98060110-4ead-4574-964f-daef0a492581","uuid":"eb6ec5f3-b0d1-43d6-b30b-1698d8690d92","timestamp":"2026-11-06T13:02:30.326Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162030__x07393c/work/PLAN.md","content":"- Men you were paid to kill\n- Friends lost\n- Stones earned\n\nWritten as Harrow would write it.\n\n**Saving:** single slot, versioned JSON in `localStorage` (`src/core/save.js`), written on sleep and on mission complete, read through `ctx.input.send` so replays stay exact. Main menu's Continue loads it. Dev mode has Quick Save/Load.\n\n---\n\n## 14. Missions\n\n**Format** (`src/content/missions.js`), a sketch:\n```js\n{ id:'m3', title:'FUEL FOR THE PEACE', giver:'vance', requires:['m2'], pay:15, wind:{ dir:[-0.8,-0.6], speed:5 },\n  brief:['vance:m3.brief.1','vance:m3.brief.2'],\n  alt:{ buddy:'ines', call:'ines:m3.alt', bonus:5, steps:[ {do:'steal',tag:'tanker',text:'TAKE THE TANKER AT P3'} ] },\n  steps:[ {do:'goto',site:'east-siding',r:140,text:'REACH THE SIDING'},\n          {do:'destroy',tag:'fuel-tank',n:3,text:'BURN THE TANKS'},\n          {do:'leave',site:'east-siding',r:220,text:'GET OUT'},\n          {do:'report',to:'vance',text:'REPORT TO VANCE'} ],\n  onDone:[ {burnStrip:'A'}, {ledger:{paid:15}} ] }\n```\n**Step types:** `goto leave talk report use deliver destroy kill collect steal hold escort ride timer choice script`. A step shows its `text` for 5 s at the top when it starts, and always in the map margin. Bots drive these same steps.\n\nContracts are taken in person (a short FP scene: the camera holds on the giver, subtitles, then Accept or Not Yet) or through the notice board in Mile Forty. After M2, the order within M3/M4 and M5/M6 is free; M5 needs M3 and M6 needs M4 (one faction's path each); M7 needs all four. Acts, for the fever's pace: act 1 is M0 to M2, act 2 is M3 to M6, act 3 is M7 onward.\n\n| # | Title (giver) | Length, time | What happens | Teaches | Alternate plan | Consequence, pay |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| M0 | The Goods Line | 2 min, dusk, skippable | You ride Old Bakr's flatcar into the Kettle as he talks. Prompt: raise the map (must do). The margin note. Fever on the platform; you fall | Look, map | - | Fade to the clinic |\n| M1 | Mercy Run (Odile) | 7 min, morning | Wake at the clinic. Take a tablet. Given an old `tractor` (cond 45). Drive medicine to Three Wells. On the way back P2 is manned. The 5th shot **jams by script**; then the truck is hit and stalls: repair. Syrette. Report | Walk, use, tablet, drive, waypoint, fire, jam, reload, syrette, repair | - | +3 tablets, 5 stones, Pump Shed |\n| M2 | A Cage at the Post (Tibor) | 7 min, best at night | Ines owes Tibor. She's in a cage at Ranger Post (8 Concord, a tower). Scout with the monocular, cross in grass, cane knife, or go loud. Open the cage (hold). Ines fights her way out with you. She explains rescues by doing one if you fall | Monocular, stealth, melee, sleep to choose the hour, safehouse capture, buddy | - | Ranger Post safehouse, 8 stones, Ines |\n| M3 | Fuel for the Peace (Vance) | 7 min | Burn the Harvest's 3 tanks at East Siding. Vance hands you the flare pistol. Wind pinned toward the depot: the grass will carry fire if you start it upwind | Flare, wind, fire, chain explosions | Ines: steal the tanker at P3 and drive it in; soldiers hold fire until you're inside | Scar A, 15 stones (+5). A column of smoke visible across the map for a game day |\n| M4 | Seed Money (Ansa) | 7 min | Payroll convoy (2 technicals, a truck) crosses the Salt Pan on a loop. Stop it, take the case. It flies out when the truck blows: you get the tracker to find it in the salt | Vehicle combat, MG, tracker | Dov: plant his charges on the bridge, detonate as the convoy crosses | 20 stones (+5), tracker, Dov |\n| M5 | The Water Question (Vance) | 7 min | Destroy the pump on the Mercy, because Three Wells \"feeds the Harvest\" | Charges, defending, moral cost | Mags: first open the bypass and hold the pump house for 60 s, so the cistern fills | Without alt: Three Wells empties, a line of people walks the road to the clinic, its huts go dark, Odile refuses tablets until you do a Mercy Run free. With alt: village stays, pay 10 instead of 20 |\n| M6 | The Long Field (Ansa) | 9 min, forced night | Burn the Concord's crop and its ammo bunker. Your highest-trust buddy comes along (with no buddy alive, a Harvest guide named Pell does). At about 70% the wind turns (scripted) and they go down on fire: **Syrette or Finish It** | Night fire, buddy choice | The mission itself | Scar B, 25 stones, the Ledger's first hard line |\n| M7 | The Cut (Harrow's note) | 10 min | A note at your safehouse: *You have drawn well. Come and see.* Truce collapses: both armies fight for the mine. Reach the sluice house through crossfire and wildfire, take his ledger. In it: *One contractor, paid in advance, to walk the Kettle.* Signed by him | Three-way fight, technical MG, big fire | A surviving buddy calls: they hold the east road if you go in from the pit side (no bonus stones, +1 trust) | Scar C. Truce over: Mile Forty loses its no-fire zone, Tibor moves his stock into safehouse lockers. Act 2 fever pace |\n| M8 | Last Train (Odile) | 7 min | Mile Forty under shells. Hold the platform 120 s while people board. Then ride Old Bakr's train to East Siding on a flatcar MG, 60 s, on rails, under fire. *He says the grass won't burn twice.* The column starts walking the scar | Defence, on-rails MG | - | Column on the map, moving slowly and visibly along the scar |\n| M9 | The Surveyor | 10 min, night, storm | Climb to the Observatory (deserters from both armies; no fires, it's raining). Harrow sits at a table with a lamp, as sick as you. The scene: he lays your contract map down; the three scars glow as one line; he draws the last stroke. He offers tablets and the minefield sheet, and asks you to finish your contract, or not | Choice | - | `choice` steps: shoot him or don't (a Ledger line, no other effect). Then who gets the sheet |\n| End | The Pass | 3 to 4 min | Either walk to the Pass alone, or take the sheet to the column and hold behind them. Surviving buddies arrive (200 HP, real AI, last lines), with pursuit from both armies. Rain stops. The last grass is yours to light | Everything | - | Ending card, Ledger, credits, title. Continue returns to the last safehouse for free roam |\n\n**Story scars.** On completing M3, M6 and M7, call `burnStrip('A'|'B'|'C')` so the arc exists whatever the player actually burned: A from East Siding west to the Cut, C across the Cut, B from the Cut west through the Long Field to the Pass road. The player sees it first in M9.\n\n**Ending cards:**\n- **Walk out:** *You reached the border with a case of stones and a map nobody else will ever use. The guard asks your trade. You tell him: surveyor.*\n- **Give it to them:** *They crossed at first light, walking on ash. Nobody has asked who lit it. The fever is not finished with you, and you are out of tablets. It is a good view.*\n\n**Attract, tests and dev mode** can jump to any mission start: each mission has a `setup` that puts the world in the right state (`world.reset`, story flags, scars, buddies, loadout), so `dev.startMission('m6')` is one call.\n\n---\n\n## 15. Writing\n\n**Voice.** Weary, literary and exact. Short declarative sentences. Euphemism as cruelty. Gallows humour without a wink. Nobody explains the theme. Nobody is your friend without a price. People are tired, and they're smart. Think of a war correspondent who stopped filing years ago. Don't quote real authors, and don't imitate the source's lines.\n\nEach mission gets 8 to 15 spoken lines in this voice. Each character has a tic: **Vance** invoices (*conclude, regrettable, the matter of*). **Ansa** corrects grammar. **Odile** counts things. **Tibor** talks about returns. **Bakr** tells you what stations used to be called. **Ines** owes people, or they owe her. **Dov** tells a three-sentence story that ends badly. **Mags** narrates what she is doing to you. **Harrow** writes like a surveyor's notebook.\n\nAll game text must be in the HUD font's character set. Subtitle lines stay under 60 characters, two lines at most: split long sentences across lines in sequence.\n\nUse these lines verbatim, and write the rest to match:\n\n- **Bakr, M0:** *Forty miles of track and not one station that remembers its name.* / *They paint the signs over. Whoever won last.* / *You have the look of a man who read about this place. Reading is a good way to visit.* / *Up there they will ask you which side. Say yes.*\n- **Odile:** *Three tablets. The fourth you pay for. I do not mean in stones.* / *I do not need you to be good. I need you to be on time.* / *Sixty-one beds. Forty blankets. You are the math.*\n- **Vance:** *We do not burn villages. We conclude them.* / *The water question has been a great sorrow to this office.* / *Your invoice will be honoured, regrettably.*\n- **Ansa:** *You said less people. Fewer. Fewer people. It will matter by the end of the month.* / *Burn the field. A hungry man learns to read the wind.*\n- **Tibor:** *Everything on this rack has been returned at least once.* / *It fires. If you want it to fire twice, that is a different price.*\n- **Ines:** *I flew for both of them. Neither paid. Get in.* / *You owe me a truck. You owe me several trucks.*\n- **Dov:** *Two fingers I left in this country. I came back to see what they are doing.* / *A man asked me to mine his own road, so he would know where it was safe. He was right for a week.*\n- **Mags:** *Hold still. No, you can't feel that. No, that's normal. Hold still.* / *Not today. Today you owe me money.*\n- **A burning buddy:** *Don't let it be the fire. Please. Not the fire.*\n- **Barks:** *There! In the grass!* / *Who lit that?* / *It's stuck! It's stuck again!* / *Leave him, he's already gone.*\n- **Harrow's margin notes,** one per trig point, in order:\n  1. *A map is a promise made by someone who has already left.*\n  2. *I drew the river where the Company wanted it. The river was slow to comply, but it came round.*\n  3. *Both armies buy from me. The Concord pays on time. The Harvest pays in grain and tears. I have eaten better on the tears.*\n  4. *You will have noticed that you follow roads. I drew those too.*\n  5. *Grass is the only honest border. It goes where the wind tells it, and it keeps a record.*\n  6. *By now you have burned what I marked. Look at it from the ridge. Tell me that is not a line.*\n- **Harrow, M9:** *You are late. I said you would be. Sit down, it won't take long, neither of us has long.* / *I drew the lines that started this. I would like to draw one more.* / *You have been drawing for me. Look at it.* / *Burned grass cannot burn twice. It is the only safe road in the country, and you built it for wages.*\n- **Load-screen epigraphs** (*from Harrow's field notes*): write 12 in the same voice.\n\n---\n\n## 16. UI and UX\n\n**10-foot and controller first.** A PS5 DualSense on a TV at ten feet is the design target. Mouse and keyboard play the same game on the same screens and feel native. Everything is drawn with `ctx.hud` in art pixels; there is no DOM UI at all, so it all works in Node tests. Test the view at 1920×1080.\n\n**Layout rules:**\n- Safe area 24 px horizontal, 14 px vertical.\n- Menu items at scale 2; the smallest text anywhere is scale 1 (subtitles, prompts).\n- At most 6 items on a screen, one idea per screen.\n- No tables, no scroll lists, no web-style data screens. Long content is paged.\n- A focused item has a full-width bar in `orange` and a small marker. Move and confirm sounds.\n- Only the title and pause menus cover the view. Every other screen is in your hands or an overlay with the world visible behind it.\n\n**HUD in play is minimal** and hides 6 s after it last changed:\n- 5 health segments, syrette and tablet counts bottom-left.\n- Ammo and the gun's condition icon bottom-right.\n- A dot reticle (hidden while scoped; the scope has its own black mask).\n- Prompts centre-bottom. Subtitles above them with the speaker's name in a colour.\n- Mission step at the top for 5 s when it changes.\n\n**Controls** (`src/core/actions.js`):\n\n| Action | DualSense | Xbox glyph | Keyboard and mouse |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Move / look | L stick / R stick | same | WASD / mouse |\n| Fire / aim | R2 / L2 | RT / LT | LMB / RMB |\n| Use (when a prompt shows), else reload | Square | X | E / R |\n| Jump | Cross | A | Space |\n| Crouch | Circle | B | C (never Ctrl: Ctrl+W closes the browser tab) |\n| Sprint | L3 (click) | LS | Left Shift |\n| Melee | R3 | RS | F |\n| Next weapon | Triangle | Y | Wheel, or 1-4 |\n| Throw / plant | R1 | RB | G |\n| Syrette, surgery | L1 | LB | Q |\n| Map up / down | D-pad Up | D-pad Up | M or Tab |\n| Tablet | D-pad Down | D-pad Down | H |\n| Tracker | D-pad Left | D-pad Left | T |\n| Monocular (hold) | D-pad Right | D-pad Right | V |\n| Pause | Options | Menu | Esc |\n| Ledger | Create | View | J |\n| **Driving:** gas / brake-reverse / steer | R2 / L2 / L stick | RT / LT / L stick | W / S / A-D |\n| Handbrake | Cross | A | Space |\n| Get out / repair | Square | X | E |\n| Swap to gun | Triangle | Y | F |\n| Chase camera | R3 | RS | C |\n\nUse `input.preventKeys.add('Tab')` etc. Analog triggers: each frame, read `navigator.getGamepads()` buttons 6 and 7 `value` and `input.send({ tr:[l2, r2] })` when changed, so recordings keep it, and use it for throttle and brake. Rumble: `pad.vibrationActuator?.playEffect('dual-rumble', {...})`, guarded, Settings toggle.\n\n**Glyphs.** Prompts follow the input used last:\n- `device` flips to `kbm` on keydown, mouse button or real mouse movement, and to `pad` on any `Pad*` code or a stick past 0.35.\n- `src/ui/glyphs.js` is pixel art as `hud.sprite` rows, about 11 × 11: Cross, Circle, Square, Triangle, L1, L2, R1, R2, L3, R3, D-pad directions, Options, Create; Xbox A, B, X, Y, LB, LT, RB, RT, LS, RS, Menu, View; a key cap drawn around any letter; LMB, RMB, MMB, wheel.\n- Settings has **Glyphs: PlayStation / Xbox**, default PlayStation.\n- `game.state().prompts` lists what's on screen, so tests can check it.\n\n**The mouse is native.** In menus the pointer is free (no lock), hover moves focus, click activates (read `input.buttonEvents`; convert with `x = (p.x+1)/2*hud.width`, `y = (1-p.y)/2*hud.height`). The wheel scrolls pages. Over the world it aims and looks under pointer lock. On the held map it's a cursor (hover focuses a marker, click sets the waypoint). On Tibor's rack and in dialogue choices, click works too. Keyboard in menus: arrows or WASD, Enter or Space, Esc back. Pad in menus: D-pad or left stick with key repeat, Cross confirms, Circle goes back, L1/R1 change tabs and pages. If the pad disconnects during play, open the pause menu.\n\n**The held map** (`src/world/map-texture.js`). The heart of pillar 3.\n- 320 × 240 DataTexture on a plane about 0.5 × 0.375 m, about 0.42 m in front of the camera, tilted, in both hands (the `hand` model and hands rig), filling about 70% of the width, so one texel is about one art pixel. A 0.62 m plane, which I tried first, was too big.\n- Baked at start: contour lines every 8 m on sand paper, river, roads, rail, labels in your own 5×7 `pixfont.js`.\n- Redrawn at up to 2 Hz on a copy: burn scars (ink), your position and heading, the waypoint, sites you've seen, mission step and Harrow's notes in the margin, wind arrow and clock on a small GPS clipped to the corner.\n- Raise and lower takes 0.4 s with paper sound. **The world never stops.** You can walk and drive with it up. While it's up, the look input moves the map cursor.\n- Square/LMB on a marker sets the waypoint; Triangle or wheel toggles a closer zoom.\n- It works at night because the paper uses a dim lit toon plus a small hand torch `lights.request` following the view group.\n\n**Screens:**\n- **Loading:** the engine's, then a black screen with one Harrow epigraph.\n- **Title:** live 3D scene (dusk, fixed slow camera over burning grass on the Long Field, music), the title large (scale 4, or 3 if it won't fit), the latest input's *Press [glyph]*. Then the main menu.\n- **Main menu:** Continue (when a save exists), New Game, Cash Run, Settings, About and Credits.\n- **Pause** (`timeScale = 0`): Resume, Ledger, Settings, Dev Mode, About and Credits, Quit to Title. In a hub session: Resume and Settings only.\n- **Settings:** Sound (Music slider **default 10%**, Effects, Voices), Controls (Look sensitivity for pad, for mouse; Invert Y; Aim assist; Rumble; Glyphs), Picture (Fullscreen, for the TV; Pixel size Fine/Chunky via `engine.settings.set`; Quality; Field of view), Comfort (Subtitle size; Reduce flashes; Fever effects reduced), Reset to Defaults. Saved in your own `localStorage` entry and re-applied at boot: `settings:{ button:false, key:false }` hides the engine's panel and stops the engine saving its own copy.\n- **Dialogue:** the camera holds on the speaker; subtitles; two big buttons at most.\n- **Tibor's rack:** one gun at a time, large (its first-person model turned to the side on a table), name, three bars (Damage, Range, Reliability), price. Left/right cycles. Buy or Take.\n- **Locker:** one row per slot, left/right picks.\n- **Bed:** Dawn, Noon, Dusk, Midnight, Leave.\n- **Ledger:** section 13.\n- **Game Over, Ending card, Credits.**\n- **About and Credits:** paged, see section 27.\n\n**Touch-only devices.** Detect with `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches` and no pad connected (verified: true on Chromium with the `iPhone 14`, `iPad Pro 11` and `Pixel 7` profiles, false on a desktop context). Engine option `touch:false` always, so there are never on-screen controls. On such a device the title shows **Controller or keyboard required** (the exact text in `state().notice`, drawn uppercase by the font) and one large **Settings** button (tap works as click: `input.buttonEvents` reports a finger as code `Touch`). Attract mode still starts after 10 s; a tap exits to this screen. A key press or pad connecting clears the gate and shows the normal title.\n\n---\n\n## 17. Dev mode\n\nPause menu → **Dev Mode** (hidden in a hub session). An overlay with tabs (L1/R1 or Q/E), world visible behind, playing or frozen by a toggle.\n\n| Tab | Contents |\n| --- | --- |\n| Cheats | God mode, infinite ammo, no jams, no fever, invisible to AI, noclip fly |\n| Teleport | Every site, every post, every case, the crosshair point |\n| Spawn | Squad of each faction, pickup, technical, truck, a stone case, a buddy |\n| World | Hour slider, wind direction and speed sliders, weather (clear, dust, storm), ignite at crosshair, extinguish all, regrow all, sleep +6 h |\n| Mission | Start any mission, complete current step, set story flags, give stones, tablets, syrettes, all guns; break gun; force jam; force fever; down a buddy |\n| **Balance** | Live sliders (below), **Reset to Defaults** for all, Square/R resets one |\n| Debug | Fire-grid overlay, nav overlay, AI state text over heads, counts (actors, burning cells, draw info from `engine.state()`), engine debug panel (`engine.showDebug`), free camera (`engine.setCamera({ preset:'free' })`, restored after; re-install `step` in `onCameraChange`), crosshair coordinates for placing things in `src/content/`, Quick Save/Load, show `status()` |\n\n**Balance sliders** (left/right steps, hold accelerates, mouse drags). Defaults in `src/content/tuning-defaults.js`:\n\n| Slider | Default | Range |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `playerSpeed` multiplier | 1 | 0.5-2 |\n| `playerDamageTaken` multiplier | 1 | 0-3 |\n| `weaponDamage` multiplier | 1 | 0.25-4 |\n| `enemyHealth` multiplier | 1 | 0.25-4 |\n| `enemyAccuracy` | 1 | 0.25-3 |\n| `enemyVision` (m) | 90 | 20-200 |\n| `enemyReaction` (s) | 0.45 | 0.1-2 |\n| `wearRate` | 1 | 0-5 |\n| `jamRate` | 1 | 0-5 |\n| `fireSpread` | 1 | 0-3 |\n| `fireDamage` (HP/s) | 8 | 0-30 |\n| `windEffect` | 1 | 0-3 |\n| `feverMinutes` | 12 | 2-40 |\n| `vehicleTopSpeed` (m/s) | 26 | 10-45 |\n| `vehicleToughness` | 1 | 0.25-4 |\n| `stonesReward` multiplier | 1 | 0-5 |\n| `buddyWoundChance` | 0.15 | 0-1 |\n| `dayMinutes` | 30 | 2-120 |\n| `postRemanHours` | 24 | 1-96 |\n| `regrowHours` | 48 | 1-200 |\n\nA test sets every slider, checks the system responds, presses Reset, and checks every value equals its default.\n\n---\n\n## 18. Attract mode\n\nAfter **10 seconds with no input on the title screen or main menu**, start a looping demo (`src/attract/`). Settings and About are exempt, because people stop to read them. It's a director with a list of beats, using the real game with `cam.override`, god mode, infinite ammo and bot input through the same action layer. It cheats freely: teleports, spawns, sets the hour and wind. A `save.disabled` flag stops it touching saves.\n\nBeats (10 to 14 s each, joined by `engine.screen.cover('dither')` and `reveal`), to show as much as possible:\n1. Dusk, driving a technical down the road, first person, raising the map at the wheel.\n2. Rolling into a checkpoint, gunfight, the gun jams, slap and rack.\n3. Flare into dry grass, the wind takes it, soldiers run burning.\n4. Night, the Long Field in flames, chase camera past it.\n5. Fever: the view swims, tablet to mouth.\n6. Field surgery with pliers.\n7. Scoped shot from a ridge at noon.\n8. Dragged out by a buddy; syrette or finish it.\n9. Tracker beeping to a case in a burnt wreck.\n10. Train with the flatcar MG.\n11. Tibor's rack, a line of his.\n12. The map on a table with the scars glowing.\n13. The title.\n\nHUD shows a `DEMO` tag and *Press [glyph]*. **Any input exits** (key, mouse button or real movement, pad button or stick, tap) back to the screen it came from, after `world.reset()`. The loop must run indefinitely without error. It runs behind the touch gate too. Never in a hub session.\n\n---\n\n## 19. Multiplayer\n\nFollow the AI Hub Session Protocol v1 (read `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`; also the shared-world example `examples/arena.html` beside it). The hub runs invites, lobby, names, clock and results; the game runs the round. The same code also plays when the game is on its own.\n\n**Mode: `shared-world`, 1 to 4 players.** Four mercs in one burning valley, friends until the stones are counted.\n\n**The round, \"Cash Run\" (6 minutes):**\n- The valley around the Cut: the campaign's terrain, with only the Cut, P5 and the Ranger Post live, 16 to 24 soldiers, wind and fire on.\n- Six stone cases in guarded spots, shown by the tracker's beep and a marker when close. One extraction truck on the road south of the pit.\n- Everyone starts at a different road end with `tractor` (cond 70), `flare`, `cane`, 2 syrettes, 2 bottles.\n- Carry one case at a time (speed × 0.85, you can't sprint); walk it to the truck to bank its stones. Most stones wins.\n- Down at 0 HP: you drop the case and bleed for 25 s. Another player can hold Use for 3 s to bring you up (+1 Revive) or just take the case. Bleed out and you return at your road end after 15 s. Friendly fire is on: that's the theme.\n- On foot only, in rounds: no player vehicles.\n- Ends when the time is up, or when all cases are banked or burned. Standings by stones, ties together.\n\n**Session head tags** go in the template (section 23): `hub:session` 1, `hub:session-players` `1-4`, `hub:session-mode` `shared-world`, `hub:session-minutes` `6`, `hub:webgpu` `required`, `hub:session-goal` *Carry the most diamond cases out of the burning mine*, `hub:session-howto` *Stick/WASD move, R2/mouse fire, Square/E use, carry cases to the truck*.\n\n**Boot order** (`src/main.js`). This is the part that makes the hub work:\n```js\nconst info = (window.AIHub && AIHub.active) ? await AIHub.connect({ mode:'shared-world', seats:[1,4], card:true }) : null;\nif (info) {\n  const game = createGame({ session: hubSession(info) });        // mode 'round': no title, no menus, no attract\n  if (info.server) { const e = await Engine.headless(game, {}); AIHub.ready(); setInterval(() => e.step(6, 1/60), 100); }\n  else if (!navigator.gpu) AIHub.fail('This game needs WebGPU');\n  else await Engine.start(game, { ...OPTIONS, seed: info.seed });  // game.ready(ctx) calls AIHub.ready() once, with no key press\n} else { /* normal start: touch check, title */ }\n```\nHandle a rejected `__PIXEL_READY__` by `AIHub.fail(message)`. If `connect` answers `null`, run as on your own.\n\n**`src/net/session.js`:** one interface, three implementations, so round code never knows which: `{ kind, me, players:[{id,name,color}], host, isHost, server, time(), rng(label), send(data,{to,reliable}), on(event,fn), ready(), answer(what), finish(outcome), fail(msg) }`.\n- `hubSession` wraps `AIHub`.\n- `soloSession` is **on its own**: host is you, the other seats are AI mercs (reuse the buddy brain: go to the nearest case, bank it, shoot what shoots you), with your own results screen at the end.\n- `linkSession` is **on its own with a friend on the same computer**: `BroadcastChannel('game-link-v1')` between two windows. Host and Join on the Cash Run menu, a simple lobby, `start` carrying a `Date.now()` time base and a seed. It costs little, reuses everything, and is how two-window play gets tested.\n\nThe main menu's Cash Run offers: Solo with Hired Guns, Host on This Computer, Join on This Computer, plus one line saying friends online play through AI Hub.\n\n**Netcode.** The host runs the world. Each copy moves its own player from its own stick, at once, never waiting for the network, as `arena.html` does.\n\n| Message | Direction | Rate, kind | Content |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `me` | client → host | 12/s, unreliable | seq, position, yaw, pitch, stance, weapon, hp echo |\n| `ev` | client → host | up to 5/s, reliable, batched | shots since last batch (origin, dir, weapon), use, pick up, bank, revive, ignite |\n| `s` | host → all | 10/s, unreliable, under 1,100 bytes | time, players, soldiers (`[id,x,z,yaw,state,hp]`, ints, y from terrain), cases |\n| `w` | host → all | up to 4/s, reliable, batched | fire cells ignited and burnt, damage per player, downs, deaths, explosions, banks, sounds |\n\nThat's at most 17 messages a second per copy; the limit is 20 with bursts of 40, and 16 KB per message. **Drive sends from `setInterval`, not the render loop:** on a software-rendered copy `update` runs about twice a second, and traffic must still flow.\n\nClients render soldiers as puppets interpolated 150 ms behind; they run fire visuals only; health is host-authoritative. Local shots show muzzle flash and tracers at once, and the host decides hits. Older snapshots are dropped by `at`. In a shared world use `AIHub.rng(label)`, because `Math.random` isn't seeded there; the world is the same static terrain on all copies anyway.\n\n**The server case.** `AIHub.server` true: run the same host code under `Engine.headless` with no player, camera, audio or HUD (`me` isn't in `players`). Don't touch `info.players[me]`.\n\n**Round rules the harness checks:**\n- `time-up`: the host calls `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, stats, awards })` **directly from the event handler**, within `graceMs` (5 s). Every present player appears once.\n- `leave`: continue; the host finishes if nobody is left.\n- `end`: no more input or sends, `audio.stopMusic()`, `audio.stopLoops()`, mute. The hub shows results.\n- `stats` at most 6 names per player (Stones, Downs, Revives, Kills); `awards` up to 3 (*Last Friend* for most revives, *Paid in Full* for most stones, *Arsonist* for most cells lit).\n\n**In a session:** no title, menus or prompts before the round. No dialogs (`alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`), no `window.open`, no navigation, no network except the hub. Quit does nothing. Names come only from the hub (sanitize to the font's characters; HUD canvas, never HTML). No chat, emotes or custom names. **On a pad, ignore Options while Create is held** (Create + Options is the hub's). Sessions get an empty storage, so settings start at defaults, music at 10%.\n\n**The game's own card** (`card:true`). A shared-world card on your live scene with `GAME_TITLE`, the players in their seat colours with ready marks, how to win, this player's controls in their glyphs, time left from the `card` event. Ready: Enter, Cross, or a tap/click on Ready → `AIHub.answer('ready')`. More time: Triangle, key `M`, or tap → `AIHub.answer('more')`. It has no menus, and play begins only at `start`.\n**Listen for Enter and M with a plain `window` keydown listener** (verified to pass the harness's card check), because the harness expects an answer within 3 s and the render loop may be slow. Pad buttons can poll in `update`. Everything on the card uses `AIHub.rng('card')` for randomness. When `AIHub.time() >= 0` the round is on; show the 3-2-1 countdown before that.\n\n**Fallback.** If shared-world can't be made stable, ship `ghost` (each copy its own world, others' mercs shown, `progress` and `result` by score, `Math.random` seeded for you) rather than drop multiplayer, and last of all `parallel`.\n\n**Test it:** section 24, all four harness scenarios, and two windows on `linkSession`, plus the game outside a session.\n\n---\n\n## 20. Art\n","numLines":300,"startLine":580,"totalLines":1129}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019naJ5CYLX7f567cf5kjPDg","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
